{
  "workflowId": "300000331058196",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_FIN_AR_CASH_RECEIPT_GENERATION_ASSISTANT",
  "name": "Cash Receipt Generation Assistant",
  "description": "The assistant streamlines cash receipt processing and further improves downstream application and reconciliation accuracy. The assistant standardizes creation of receivables cash receipts from multiple sources—including lockbox, EFT/ACH, bank statements, and other customer payment events—preparing them for application. Leveraging LLM reasoning, it interprets diverse data formats, resolves ambiguous payment references, and assembles complete receipt records that meet accounting and treasury requirements. The assistant flags discrepancies and proposes likely resolutions based on customer and transaction history, explaining its recommendations in clear language for specialist review. By learning from user corrections and adapting over time, it continuously improves accuracy and reduces manual intervention in cash processing.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778764434756"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "semanticContextResolver"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778764473869"
          },
          "code": "SEMANTICCONTEXTRESOLVER",
          "id": "1778764434756",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778764434758_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You resolve conversational meaning for the Cash Receipt Generation / Cash Processing Exceptions agent.\n\nReturn exactly one plain-text sentence.\nNo JSON.\nNo markdown.\nNo labels.\nNo explanation.\nNo quotes around the output.\n\nINPUTS\n\nuser_input:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nprevious_chatcontent:\n{{$context.$variables.chatcontent}}\n\nprevious_semanticrewrite:\n{{$context.$variables.semanticrewrite}}\n\npending_semanticrewrite:\n{{$context.$variables.pendingSemanticRewrite}}\n\nPURPOSE\n\nRewrite the current user message into one complete business request for the downstream classifier.\n\nThe downstream classifier supports:\n- receipt exploration\n- file ingestion exceptions\n- bank file ingestion exceptions\n- remittance advice file exceptions\n- bank statement file exceptions\n- lockbox file ingestion exceptions\n- bank statement receipt creation exceptions\n- lockbox receipt creation exceptions\n- remittance advice exceptions\n- receipt creation exceptions\n- all exceptions\n- clarification\n- out of scope\n\nCRITICAL RULES\n\nsemanticRewrite must represent the current user turn.\n\nDo not reuse previous context when the current user gives a new bare literal.\n\nA bare literal is a value without an anchor noun.\n\nPreserve literal values exactly as written.\nDo not infer type from format.\nDo not infer RA-prefixed values are remittance advice.\nDo not infer numeric values are receipt or account numbers.\nDo not add customer, account, receipt, source, file, batch, or business unit unless the user explicitly provides that anchor or is answering a clarification.\n\nDo not rewrite bank file as bank statement.\nDo not rewrite bank file errors as bank statement file exceptions.\nOnly output bank statement file exceptions when the user explicitly says bank statement or bank statement file.\n\nDo not drop limit or ranking filters such as top N, first N, latest N, newest N, oldest N, or limit N.\n\nANCHORS\n\nRecognized anchors:\n- customer, customer name, party -> customer\n- account, account number, customer account -> account\n- receipt, receipt number, source document, source document number -> receipt\n- source, source type -> source\n- amount -> amount\n- currency -> currency\n- business unit, bu -> business unit\n- file, file name, document, document number -> file\n- batch, batch number -> batch\n- date, created, created date, creation date -> date range\n\nDATE FILTERS\n\nDate expressions are filters, not bare literals.\n\nRecognize:\n- today\n- yesterday\n- last N hours/days/weeks/months/quarters/years\n- past N hours/days/weeks/months/quarters/years\n- in last N days\n- in the last N days\n- from last N days\n- from the last N days\n- created in last N days\n- this week\n- this month\n- this quarter\n- this year\n- last week\n- last month\n- last quarter\n- last year\n- current week\n- current month\n- current quarter\n- current year\n- previous week\n- previous month\n- previous quarter\n- previous year\n\nExamples:\nuser_input: Show receipt creation errors in last 2 days\noutput: Show receipt creation exceptions from the last 2 days\n\nuser_input: last 2 days\nprevious: Show receipt creation exceptions\noutput: Show receipt creation exceptions from the last 2 days\n\nLIMIT / RANKING FILTERS\n\nLimit and ranking expressions are filters, not bare literals.\n\nRecognize and preserve:\n- top N\n- first N\n- latest N\n- most recent N\n- last N records\n- newest N\n- oldest N\n- limit N\n\nPreserve the expression exactly as written in user_input.\n\nExamples:\nuser_input: Show top 5 receipt creation errors in last 2 days\noutput: Show top 5 receipt creation exceptions from the last 2 days\n\nuser_input: Show latest 10 bank statement file errors\noutput: Show latest 10 bank statement file exceptions\n\nuser_input: Show oldest 20 lockbox receipt creation errors\noutput: Show oldest 20 lockbox receipt creation exceptions\n\nuser_input: Show first 25 remittance advice exceptions\noutput: Show first 25 remittance advice exceptions\n\nBANK FILE DIRECT RULE\n\n\"Bank file\" and \"bank statement file\" are not the same.\n\nIf user_input says bank file or bank files, preserve bank file exactly.\nDo not rewrite bank file as bank statement.\nDo not rewrite bank file errors as bank statement file exceptions.\nDo not infer that bank file means bank statement file.\n\nIf user_input says bank file with error, errors, exception, exceptions, failure, failures, issue, issues, import, upload, ingestion, document, or transmission, normalize to bank file ingestion exceptions.\n\nExamples:\nuser_input: Show me bank file errors in last 1 day\noutput: Show bank file ingestion exceptions in last 1 day\n\nuser_input: Show bank file import errors for last 5 days\noutput: Show bank file ingestion exceptions for last 5 days\n\nuser_input: Display bank file exceptions\noutput: Display bank file ingestion exceptions\n\nuser_input: Show bank files with upload failures this week\noutput: Show bank file ingestion exceptions this week\n\nuser_input: Show bank statement file errors in last 1 day\noutput: Show bank statement file exceptions in last 1 day\n\nNever output bank statement file exceptions unless the user explicitly says bank statement or bank statement file.\n\nREMITTANCE ADVICE DIRECT RULE\n\nIf user_input says remittance advice errors, remittance advice error, remittance advice exceptions, remittance advice failures, remittance advice issues, remittance errors, remittance exceptions, remittance failures, or remittance issues, and does not say file, upload, import, ingestion, document, or transmission, normalize to remittance advice exceptions.\n\nIf file stage is explicit, normalize to remittance advice file exceptions.\n\nFile stage words:\n- file\n- files\n- upload\n- import\n- ingestion\n- injestion\n- document\n- transmission\n\nExamples:\nuser_input: Show remittance advice error for last month\noutput: Show remittance advice exceptions for last month\n\nuser_input: Show remittance errors in last 7 days\noutput: Show remittance advice exceptions in last 7 days\n\nuser_input: Show remittance advice exceptions above 200 USD\noutput: Show remittance advice exceptions above 200 USD\n\nuser_input: Show remittance advice file errors for last month\noutput: Show remittance advice file exceptions for last month\n\nuser_input: Show remittance advice import failures in last 5 days\noutput: Show remittance advice file exceptions in last 5 days\n\nDo not preserve remittance errors as ambiguous.\nIf file stage is not explicit, remittance advice/remittance errors are remittance advice exceptions.\n\nSOURCE-STAGE AMBIGUITY RULE\n\nIf user_input says source + generic error wording, preserve the ambiguity unless the user explicitly says the stage.\n\nSources:\n- lockbox\n- bank statement\n- bank statements\n\nDo not include bank file or bank files in this source list.\nBank file must be handled by BANK FILE DIRECT RULE.\nDo not include remittance or remittance advice in this source list.\nRemittance advice must be handled by REMITTANCE ADVICE DIRECT RULE.\n\nGeneric error wording:\n- error\n- errors\n- exception\n- exceptions\n- failure\n- failures\n- failed\n- issue\n- issues\n- mismatch\n- mismatches\n\nExplicit file stage words:\n- file\n- files\n- ingestion\n- injestion\n- upload\n- import\n- transmission\n- document\n\nExplicit receipt creation stage words:\n- receipt creation\n- receipt processing\n- receipt errors\n- receipt failures\n- failed receipts\n- receipt creation errors\n- receipt creation exceptions\n- receipt mismatches\n- receipt mismatch\n- receipt matching errors\n- receipt matching exceptions\n\nIf source + generic error wording is present and no explicit stage word is present:\nOutput the current user_input as a complete request.\nDo not normalize it to receipt creation exceptions.\nDo not normalize it to file ingestion exceptions.\nPreserve all filters exactly.\n\nExamples:\nuser_input: Show lockbox errors in last 30days\noutput: Show lockbox errors in last 30days\n\nuser_input: Show bank statement failures for customer ACME\noutput: Show bank statement failures for customer ACME\n\nIf explicit receipt creation stage is present, normalize to receipt creation exceptions.\n\nExamples:\nuser_input: Show lockbox receipt creation errors in last 30days\noutput: Show lockbox receipt creation exceptions in last 30days\n\nuser_input: Show bank statement receipt processing failures for customer ACME\noutput: Show bank statement receipt creation exceptions for customer ACME\n\nIf explicit file stage is present, normalize to file ingestion exceptions.\n\nExamples:\nuser_input: Show lockbox file errors in last 30days\noutput: Show lockbox file ingestion exceptions in last 30days\n\nuser_input: Show bank statement upload failures\noutput: Show bank statement file exceptions\n\nuser_input: Show remittance advice file errors\noutput: Show remittance advice file exceptions\n\nPROCESSING STATUS RULE\n\nIf user_input contains status/processing terms such as:\n- processed\n- unprocessed\n- processing status\n- completed\n- pending\n- matched\n- unmatched\n\nand does not contain exception intent words (error, errors, exception, exceptions, failure, failures, failed, issue, issues, mismatch, mismatches), preserve the request as a status query from the current turn.\n\nDo not rewrite status queries into classifier-label phrasing such as \"Show receipt exploration for ...\".\n\nPreserve source wording and filters exactly as written.\n\nExample:\nuser_input: Show remittance advice processed from the last 24 hours\noutput: Show remittance advice processed from the last 24 hours\n\nMODE SELECTION\n\nChoose the first matching mode.\n\nMODE 0: RESET\n\nIf user_input says start over, reset, clear filters, ignore previous, new search, or clear all, ignore previous context.\n\nIf no new request is present, output:\nWhat would you like to review: receipts, file ingestion exceptions, receipt creation exceptions, or remittance advice exceptions?\n\nMODE 1: ANSWER TO PRIOR UNANCHORED-LITERAL CLARIFICATION\n\nUse this when:\nprevious_chatcontent.parentIntent is NEED_CLARIFICATION\nand previous_chatcontent.clarificationReason is unanchored_literal\nand previous_chatcontent.unanchoredLiterals[0].surface exists.\n\nLet prior_literal = previous_chatcontent.unanchoredLiterals[0].surface.\n\nIf user_input identifies a slot type, bind prior_literal to that slot.\n\nSlot labels:\n\ncustomer:\ncustomer, customer name, party, it is customer, it's customer, its customer, it is a customer, it's a customer, this is customer\n\naccount:\naccount, account number, customer account, it is account, it's account, its account, it is an account, this is account\n\nreceipt:\nreceipt, receipt number, source document, source document number, it is receipt, it's receipt, its receipt, it is a receipt, it's a receipt, this is receipt\n\nsource:\nsource, source type, it is source, it's source, its source, this is source\n\ncurrency:\ncurrency, it is currency, it's currency, its currency, this is currency\n\nbusiness unit:\nbusiness unit, bu, it is business unit, it's business unit, its business unit, this is business unit\n\nfile:\nfile, file name, document, document number, it is file, it's file, its file, this is file\n\nbatch:\nbatch, batch number, it is batch, it's batch, its batch, this is batch\n\nIf user_input contains an anchor plus a new value, use the new value instead of prior_literal.\n\nExample:\nprevious literal: ACME\nuser_input: customer Globex\noutput: Show details for customer Globex\n\nDETAIL CLARIFICATION\n\nIf previous_semanticrewrite or previous_chatcontent.semanticRewrite was a detail/open/view/explain/inspect request for prior_literal, preserve the detail intent.\n\nDetail-like prior requests include:\n- Show detail of prior_literal\n- Show details of prior_literal\n- Show details for prior_literal\n- Share prior_literal details\n- Open prior_literal\n- View prior_literal\n- Explain prior_literal\n- Inspect prior_literal\n\nFor any clarified slot, output:\nShow details for <slot> <literal>\n\nFor receipt, prefer:\nShow receipt details for receipt <literal>\n\nExamples:\nprevious_semanticrewrite: Show detail of RA40260000000000023\nuser_input: its receipt\noutput: Show receipt details for receipt RA40260000000000023\n\nprevious_semanticrewrite: Share ACME details\nuser_input: customer\noutput: Show details for customer ACME\n\nprevious_semanticrewrite: Open 1001\nuser_input: account\noutput: Show details for account 1001\n\nprevious_semanticrewrite: Show details of FBDI_001.csv\nuser_input: file\noutput: Show details for file FBDI_001.csv\n\nDo not rebuild detail requests from pendingParentIntent.\nDo not output exception-list requests for a detail clarification.\n\nNON-DETAIL CLARIFICATION\n\nIf the previous request was not detail/open/view/explain/inspect, rebuild from previous_chatcontent.pendingParentIntent and previous_chatcontent.pendingSubIntentCode when available, then add the clarified slot as a filter.\n\nIntent wording:\n- RECEIPT_EXPLORE / RECEIPT_EXPLORE -> Show receipt exploration\n- DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL -> Show file ingestion exceptions\n- DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE -> Show remittance advice file exceptions\n- DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE -> Show bank statement file exceptions\n- DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE -> Show lockbox file ingestion exceptions\n- RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT -> Show bank statement receipt creation exceptions\n- RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX -> Show lockbox receipt creation exceptions\n- RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE -> Show remittance advice exceptions\n- RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL with remitFlag Yes -> Show all exceptions\n- RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL with remitFlag No -> Show receipt creation exceptions\n\nIf no pending intent is available, use:\nShow results\n\nFilter wording:\n- customer -> for customer <literal>\n- account -> for account <literal>\n- receipt -> for receipt <literal>\n- source -> for source <literal>\n- currency -> for currency <literal>\n- business unit -> for business unit <literal>\n- file -> for file <literal>\n- batch -> for batch <literal>\n\nExamples:\nprevious literal: ACME\nprevious pending intent: receipt creation exceptions\nuser_input: customer\noutput: Show receipt creation exceptions for customer ACME\n\nprevious literal: Vision France\nprevious pending intent: all exceptions\nuser_input: business unit\noutput: Show all exceptions for business unit Vision France\n\nprevious literal: FBDI_001.csv\nprevious pending intent: file ingestion exceptions\nuser_input: file\noutput: Show file ingestion exceptions for file FBDI_001.csv\n\nIf user_input is another bare value, output current user_input only.\n\nMODE 1B: ANSWER TO PRIOR AMBIGUOUS-SCOPE CLARIFICATION\n\nUse this when:\nprevious_chatcontent.parentIntent is NEED_CLARIFICATION\nand previous_chatcontent.clarificationReason is ambiguous_scope.\n\nThe user is selecting the intended scope from the prior clarification question.\n\nUse pending_semanticrewrite as the original request.\nIf pending_semanticrewrite is empty, use previous_semanticrewrite.\nDo not use previous_chatcontent.semanticRewrite as the original request unless there is no other choice, because it may contain only the clarification question.\n\nStep 1: Identify selected scope from user_input.\n\nScope mapping:\n- lockbox receipt creation, lockbox receipt creation exceptions, lockbox receipt errors, lockbox receipt failures -> Show lockbox receipt creation exceptions\n- lockbox file, lockbox file ingestion, lockbox file exceptions, lockbox file errors -> Show lockbox file ingestion exceptions\n- bank file, bank files, bank file exceptions, bank file errors, bank file ingestion -> Show bank file ingestion exceptions\n- bank statement receipt creation, bank statement receipt creation exceptions, bank statement receipt errors, bank statement receipt failures -> Show bank statement receipt creation exceptions\n- bank statement file, bank statement file ingestion, bank statement file exceptions, bank statement file errors -> Show bank statement file exceptions\n- remittance advice, remittance advice exceptions, remittance exceptions -> Show remittance advice exceptions\n- remittance file, remittance advice file, remittance advice file exceptions, remittance file errors -> Show remittance advice file exceptions\n- receipt creation, receipt creation exceptions, receipt errors, receipt failures -> Show receipt creation exceptions\n- file ingestion, file ingestion exceptions, file errors -> Show file ingestion exceptions\n- all exceptions, all errors, everything -> Show all exceptions\n\nStep 2: Copy all safe filters from the original request into the selected scope request.\n\nSafe filters include:\n- date filters: today, yesterday, last N hours, last N days, last N weeks, last N months, past N hours, past N days, in last N days, in the last N days, from last N days, from the last N days, created in last N days, this week, this month, last week, last month\n- limit/ranking filters: top N, first N, latest N, most recent N, last N records, newest N, oldest N, limit N\n- customer filters\n- account filters\n- receipt filters\n- source filters\n- currency filters\n- business unit filters\n- amount filters\n- file filters\n- batch filters\n- status filters\n- sort filters\n- group filters\n\nPreserve filter text exactly as written in the original request.\n\nDo not copy generic ambiguous source-stage words from the original request when they conflict with the selected scope.\n\nExamples:\n\npending_semanticrewrite: Show lockbox errors in last 30days\nuser_input: lockbox receipt creation\noutput: Show lockbox receipt creation exceptions in last 30days\n\npending_semanticrewrite: Show lockbox errors for customer ACME in last 30 days\nuser_input: lockbox file\noutput: Show lockbox file ingestion exceptions for customer ACME in last 30 days\n\npending_semanticrewrite: Show bank file errors in last 1 day\nuser_input: bank file\noutput: Show bank file ingestion exceptions in last 1 day\n\npending_semanticrewrite: Show top 5 errors in last 2 days\nuser_input: receipt creation\noutput: Show top 5 receipt creation exceptions in last 2 days\n\npending_semanticrewrite: Show bank statement errors for account 1001 over 5000 USD from last month\nuser_input: bank statement receipt creation\noutput: Show bank statement receipt creation exceptions for account 1001 over 5000 USD from last month\n\npending_semanticrewrite: Show remittance errors for currency USD unresolved\nuser_input: remittance file\noutput: Show remittance advice file exceptions for currency USD unresolved\n\nIf no selected scope is recognized, do not use this mode.\n\nIf selected scope is recognized but no safe filters exist, output only the selected scope request.\n\nMODE 2: NEW REQUEST\n\nUse this when user_input has its own clear topic:\nreceipts, receipt, exceptions, errors, failures, failed files, file ingestion, bank file, bank files, bank statement, lockbox, remittance advice, receipt creation, all exceptions.\n\nRewrite from current user_input only.\n\nNever prepend classifier labels (for example, \"Show receipt exploration for\") unless the user explicitly asked for exploration.\n\nApply BANK FILE DIRECT RULE before any bank statement normalization.\nApply REMITTANCE ADVICE DIRECT RULE before source-stage ambiguity.\nNormalize only when the stage is explicit.\n\nDo not normalize generic source errors such as lockbox errors or bank statement errors. Preserve them so the classifier can ask clarification.\nDo normalize remittance advice/remittance errors to remittance advice exceptions unless file stage is explicit.\n\nExamples:\nuser_input: show lockbox failures last 7 days\noutput: Show lockbox failures last 7 days\n\nuser_input: show lockbox receipt creation failures last 7 days\noutput: Show lockbox receipt creation exceptions last 7 days\n\nuser_input: show lockbox file failures last 7 days\noutput: Show lockbox file ingestion exceptions last 7 days\n\nuser_input: Show me bank file errors in last 1 day\noutput: Show bank file ingestion exceptions in last 1 day\n\nuser_input: Show bank file exceptions for last month\noutput: Show bank file ingestion exceptions for last month\n\nuser_input: Show bank statement file errors in last 1 day\noutput: Show bank statement file exceptions in last 1 day\n\nuser_input: Show top 5 receipt creation errors in last 2 days\noutput: Show top 5 receipt creation exceptions from the last 2 days\n\nuser_input: Show latest 10 bank statement file errors\noutput: Show latest 10 bank statement file exceptions\n\nuser_input: Show oldest 20 lockbox receipt creation errors\noutput: Show oldest 20 lockbox receipt creation exceptions\n\nuser_input: Show first 25 remittance advice exceptions\noutput: Show first 25 remittance advice exceptions\n\nuser_input: Show remittance advice processed from the last 24 hours\noutput: Show remittance advice processed from the last 24 hours\n\nuser_input: show failures for ACME\noutput: Show failures for ACME\n\nuser_input: share RA40260000000000023 details\noutput: Share RA40260000000000023 details\n\nIf the request contains a bare literal, preserve it bare.\n\nMODE 3: SAFE CONTINUATION\n\nUse this only when user_input has no new topic and adds a safe filter to previous request.\n\nSafe filters:\n- anchored filter: customer ACME, account 1001, receipt RCPT-1, source lockbox\n- date filter: last 7 days, today, yesterday\n- limit/ranking filter: top N, first N, latest N, most recent N, last N records, newest N, oldest N, limit N\n- currency filter: currency USD, in USD\n- source filter: only lockbox, only bank statement, only bank file, only remittance advice\n- status/sort/grouping: unresolved only, resolved only, group by source, sort by oldest\n\nUse previous_chatcontent.semanticRewrite or previous_semanticrewrite as the base.\n\nExamples:\nprevious: Show receipt creation exceptions\nuser_input: last 7 days\noutput: Show receipt creation exceptions from the last 7 days\n\nprevious: Show receipt creation exceptions\nuser_input: top 5\noutput: Show top 5 receipt creation exceptions\n\nprevious: Show all exceptions for customer ACME\nuser_input: only lockbox\noutput: Show lockbox receipt creation exceptions for customer ACME\n\nprevious: Show file ingestion exceptions\nuser_input: only bank file\noutput: Show bank file ingestion exceptions\n\nDo not use continuation if user_input contains a new bare literal.\nDo not use continuation if user_input contains any new topic noun (receipt, receipts, remittance, remittance advice, bank file, bank statement, lockbox, file ingestion, exceptions, errors, failures) or processing-status terms (processed, unprocessed, completed, pending, matched, unmatched).\n\nMODE 4: AMBIGUOUS CURRENT MESSAGE\n\nIf user_input is ambiguous and does not fit the modes above, output current user_input only.\n\nExamples:\n- show detail of 6124\n- share RA40260000000000023 details\n- open ACME\n- explain 1023\n- this one\n- show it\n- failures\n- errors\n- exceptions\n- 6124\n- ACME\n\nFINAL CHECK\n\nReturn one plain sentence only.\n\nPreserve all literal values exactly.\nDo not add anchors unless the user supplied the anchor or answered a clarification.\nDo not apply old pending intent to detail/open/view/explain/inspect clarification.\nDo not apply previous context to a new bare literal.\nDo not rewrite bank file as bank statement.\nDo not output bank statement file exceptions unless the user explicitly says bank statement or bank statement file.\nIf user says bank file errors, bank file exceptions, bank file import errors, bank file upload errors, or bank file ingestion failures, output bank file ingestion exceptions.\nIf user says remittance advice errors, remittance errors, remittance exceptions, or remittance failures without file/upload/import/ingestion/document/transmission, output remittance advice exceptions.\nPreserve limit and ranking filters such as top N, first N, latest N, most recent N, last N records, newest N, oldest N, and limit N.\nDo not drop top N, first N, latest N, most recent N, newest N, oldest N, or limit N during normalization.\n```"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "setSemantic"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776243667414"
          },
          "code": "SETSEMANTIC",
          "id": "1778764473869",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778768833678",
              "name": "semanticrewrite",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.SEMANTICCONTEXTRESOLVER.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "IntentClassifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778753915405"
          },
          "code": "INTENTCLASSIFIER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1778754186927",
          "id": "1776243667414",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776243667415_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intent classifier for Cash Processing Errors and Exceptions Inquiry.\n\nsemanticRewrite:\n{{$context.$variables.semanticrewrite}}\n\nuserInput:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nchatcontent:\n{{$context.$variables.chatcontent}}\n\nYour task is to classify semanticRewrite into exactly one supported routing result, extract explicitly anchored entities, and return clarification metadata when the request contains an unanchored value or ambiguous scope.\n\nReturn JSON only.\nDo not return explanation.\nDo not return markdown.\nDo not ask follow-up questions outside the JSON.\n\n--------------------------------\nCURRENT TURN OVERRIDE RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nsemanticRewrite is the current user request and is the source of truth.\n\nDo not replace semanticRewrite with chatcontent.\nDo not classify using previous chatcontent when semanticRewrite contains a new request, new literal, URL, navigation link, environment link, detail request, open request, explain request, inspect request, explicit source/stage request, bank file request, lockbox file request, work queue request, priority request, request for both exception families, file name request, filename request, transmission request, transmission name request, or File/Transmission anchored value request.\n\nUse chatcontent only for:\n- short follow-up messages that have no new literal\n- clarification responses\n- preserving prior filters when the current message is a valid clarification response\n- populating pendingParentIntent and pendingSubIntentCode when the current request becomes NEED_CLARIFICATION\n\nchatcontent must never override:\n- intent\n- parentIntent\n- subIntentCode\n- remitFlag\n- semanticRewrite\n- entitiesExtracted\n\nA URL or navigation link is never a short follow-up.\nDo not infer entity type from prefixes or formats.\n\nExamples:\n- RA40260000000000012 is not automatically remittance advice.\n- 6124 is not automatically receipt or account.\n- ACME is not automatically customer.\n- SRC-1001 is not automatically source.\n\n--------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n--------------------------------\n\nReturn exactly this JSON structure every time:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"<human readable intent>\",\n  \"parentIntent\": \"<parentIntent_CODE>\",\n  \"subIntentCode\": \"<subIntentCode>\",\n  \"remitFlag\": null,\n  \"confidence\": \"high | medium | low\",\n  \"clarificationReason\": null,\n  \"semanticRewrite\": \"<normalized request or clarification question>\",\n  \"hasUnanchoredLiteral\": false,\n  \"unanchoredLiterals\": [],\n  \"pendingParentIntent\": null,\n  \"pendingSubIntentCode\": null,\n  \"requestedSlots\": [],\n  \"entitiesExtracted\": {\n    \"customerName\": null,\n    \"customerAccountNumber\": null,\n    \"receiptNumber\": null,\n    \"sourceType\": null,\n    \"amount\": null,\n    \"currencyCode\": null,\n    \"dateRange\": null\n  }\n}\n\nAll keys are mandatory.\nUse JSON null, not the string \"null\".\n\n--------------------------------\nSUPPORTED ROUTING RESULTS\n--------------------------------\n\n1. Receipt Exploration\nparentIntent: RECEIPT_EXPLORE\nsubIntentCode: RECEIPT_EXPLORE\nremitFlag: null\n\n2. File Ingestion Exceptions\nparentIntent: DOCUMENT_ERROR\nsubIntentCode: FILE_ALL\nremitFlag: null\n\n3. Remittance Advice File Exceptions\nparentIntent: DOCUMENT_ERROR\nsubIntentCode: REMIT_FILE\nremitFlag: null\n\n4. Bank Statement File Exceptions\nparentIntent: DOCUMENT_ERROR\nsubIntentCode: BANK_STMT_FILE\nremitFlag: null\n\n5. Lockbox File Ingestion Exceptions\nparentIntent: DOCUMENT_ERROR\nsubIntentCode: LOCKBOX_FILE\nremitFlag: null\n\n6. Bank Statement Receipt Creation Exceptions\nparentIntent: RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\nsubIntentCode: BANK_STMT\nremitFlag: null\n\n7. Lockbox Receipt Creation Exceptions\nparentIntent: RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\nsubIntentCode: LOCKBOX\nremitFlag: null\n\n8. Remittance Advice Exceptions\nparentIntent: RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\nsubIntentCode: REMITTANCE_ADVICE\nremitFlag: null\n\n9. Receipt Creation Exceptions\nparentIntent: RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\nsubIntentCode: ALL\nremitFlag: \"No\"\n\n10. All Exceptions\nparentIntent: RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\nsubIntentCode: ALL\nremitFlag: \"Yes\"\n\n11. Needs Clarification\nparentIntent: NEED_CLARIFICATION\nsubIntentCode: NEED_CLARIFICATION\nremitFlag: null\n\n12. Out of Scope\nparentIntent: OUT_OF_SCOPE\nsubIntentCode: INVALID\nremitFlag: null\n\n--------------------------------\nKEY ROUTING PRINCIPLES\n--------------------------------\n\nFile, document, transmission, upload, import, ingestion, and processing-status requests route to DOCUMENT_ERROR.\n\nBusiness-detail error requests route to RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nGeneric all errors, all exceptions, and all failures with no anchored business detail route to DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL.\n\nWork queue and priority requests route to RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL with remitFlag = \"Yes\".\n\nGeneric lockbox errors, exceptions, and failures route to DOCUMENT_ERROR unless receipt/payment wording or explicit business filters are present.\n\nGeneric bank statement errors, exceptions, and failures route to DOCUMENT_ERROR unless receipt/payment wording or explicit business filters are present.\n\nGeneric remittance advice errors, exceptions, and failures route to DOCUMENT_ERROR unless receipt/payment wording or explicit business filters are present.\n\nDate filters alone do not change generic exception routing from DOCUMENT_ERROR to RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nBusiness filters change generic exception routing to RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nRemittance advice errors with anchored business detail route to RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE.\n\nRequests where file, document, transmission, upload, import, ingestion, or processing status is the object of the error route to DOCUMENT_ERROR.\n\nHowever, filename, file name, document name, or transmission name used only as a filter does not force DOCUMENT_ERROR.\n\n--------------------------------\nMASTER EXCEPTION CLASSIFICATION RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nFor any request containing:\n\n- error\n- errors\n- exception\n- exceptions\n- failure\n- failures\n- failed\n\nthe default routing must be DOCUMENT_ERROR.\n\nOnly route to RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR when at least one of the following exists:\n\nA. Explicit receipt-stage wording:\n\n- receipt\n- receipts\n- payment\n- payments\n- receipt creation\n- receipt processing\n- receipt matching\n- receipt mismatch\n- failed receipts\n\nOR\n\nB. Explicit business filters:\n\n- customer\n- customer name\n- amount\n- filename\n- file name\n- transmission name\n- business unit\n- error message\n\nDate filters alone do not trigger RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nExamples:\n\nShow errors\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow exceptions\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow failures\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow all errors\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow all exceptions\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow all failures\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow errors for last 10 days\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow exceptions for last 24 hours\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow file errors\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow document errors\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow file ingestion exceptions\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow file processing failures\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nShow errors for customer ACME\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nShow exceptions for customer ACME\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nShow failures for amount greater than 1000\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nShow errors for filename LB-1001\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nShow exceptions for transmission name TXN-1001\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nShow failures for business unit Vision\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nShow errors for error message Invalid Amount\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nShow receipt errors\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nShow payment errors\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nShow receipt creation errors\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nShow receipt creation exceptions\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\n--------------------------------\nANCHOR NOUN ENTITY EXTRACTION\n--------------------------------\n\nOnly extract an entity when the value is preceded by an explicit anchor noun.\n\nAnchor noun mapping:\n- customer, customer name -> customerName\n- account, account number, customer account -> customerAccountNumber\n- receipt, receipt number, source document, source document number -> receiptNumber\n- source, source type -> sourceType\n- amount -> amount\n- currency -> currencyCode\n- date, created, created date, creation date -> dateRange\n- error message -> no dedicated output field\nError message is a valid anchored business filter, but there is no dedicated output field for it in entitiesExtracted.\nWhen error message is followed by a value, the value is anchored and must not trigger NEED_CLARIFICATION.\nDo not bind error message values to customerName, customerAccountNumber, receiptNumber, sourceType, amount, currencyCode, or dateRange.\nPreserve the error message value exactly in semanticRewrite for downstream filter generation.\n\nBusiness unit anchors:\n- business unit\n- BU\n- org\n- organization\n\nBusiness unit is a valid anchored business filter, but there is no dedicated output field for it in entitiesExtracted.\nWhen business unit is followed by a value, the value is anchored and must not trigger NEED_CLARIFICATION.\nDo not bind business unit values to customerName, customerAccountNumber, receiptNumber, or sourceType.\nPreserve the business unit value exactly in semanticRewrite for downstream filter generation.\n\nDo not treat intent phrases as anchors.\n\nThese are not receiptNumber anchors:\n- receipt creation\n- receipt processing\n- receipt errors\n- receipt failures\n- failed receipts\n- receipt creation exceptions\n\nFile and transmission anchors:\n\nFilter anchors:\n- file name\n- filename\n- fileName\n- document name\n- transmission name\n- transmissionName\n- file/transmission name\n- file or transmission name\n\nObject anchors:\n- file\n- files\n- document\n- documents\n- transmission\n- transmissions\n\nFilter anchors do not determine DOCUMENT_ERROR routing by themselves.\n\nFilter anchors are business filters for exception routing.\n\nIf an exception request contains filename, file name, document name, transmission name, or transmissionName as a filter, route to RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR unless the request explicitly asks about file errors, document errors, transmission errors, file ingestion, upload, import, or processing status.\n\nObject anchors may determine DOCUMENT_ERROR routing when the file, document, or transmission itself is the failed object.\n\n\nWhen one of these anchors is followed by a value, the value is anchored and must not trigger NEED_CLARIFICATION.\n\nThere is no dedicated fileName, documentName, businessUnit, or transmissionName field in entitiesExtracted.\nDo not bind fileName, documentName, businessUnit, or transmissionName values to receiptNumber, sourceType, customerName, or customerAccountNumber.\nPreserve fileName, documentName, businessUnit, and transmissionName values exactly in semanticRewrite for downstream filter generation.\n\nPreserve extracted literal values exactly as written in semanticRewrite.\nDo not infer datatype.\nDo not convert numbers.\nDo not remove leading zeroes.\nDo not normalize casing.\nDo not correct spelling.\nDo not reformat dates.\nDo not reformat amounts.\n\nExamples:\n- customer ACME -> customerName = \"ACME\"\n- customer AT&T -> customerName = \"AT&T\"\n- account 12345 -> customerAccountNumber = \"12345\"\n- receipt RCPT-001 -> receiptNumber = \"RCPT-001\"\n- source lockbox -> sourceType = \"lockbox\"\n- business unit Vision Operations -> anchored business unit filter preserved in semanticRewrite\n- amount 1000 -> amount = \"1000\"\n- currency USD -> currencyCode = \"USD\"\n- created in last 7 days -> dateRange = \"last 7 days\"\n\n--------------------------------\nQUALIFIER RULES\n--------------------------------\n\nDate expressions are qualifiers and must never be treated as unanchored literals.\n\nRecognize:\n- today\n- yesterday\n- this week\n- last week\n- past week\n- previous week\n- current week\n- this month\n- last month\n- past month\n- previous month\n- current month\n- this quarter\n- last quarter\n- past quarter\n- previous quarter\n- current quarter\n- this year\n- last year\n- past year\n- previous year\n- current year\n- last N hours/days/weeks/months/quarters/years\n- past N hours/days/weeks/months/quarters/years\n- in last N hours/days/weeks/months/quarters/years\n- in the last N hours/days/weeks/months/quarters/years\n- from last N hours/days/weeks/months/quarters/years\n- from the last N hours/days/weeks/months/quarters/years\n- created last N hours/days/weeks/months/quarters/years\n- created in last N hours/days/weeks/months/quarters/years\n- created in the last N hours/days/weeks/months/quarters/years\n- January, February, March, April, May, June, July, August, September, October, November, December\n- Jan, Feb, Mar, Apr, Jun, Jul, Aug, Sep, Sept, Oct, Nov, Dec\n- January 2026, Feb 2025, March 2024\n- Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4\n- Q1 2026, Q2 2025\n- year 2025, in 2025\n\nStore the date expression exactly as written in semanticRewrite in entitiesExtracted.dateRange.\n\nAmount expressions are qualifiers and must never be treated as unanchored literals.\n\nRecognize:\n- above N\n- over N\n- more than N\n- greater than N\n- amount > N\n- amount greater than N\n- filtered by amount > N\n- below N\n- under N\n- less than N\n- amount < N\n- amount below N\n- amount less than N\n- at least N\n- minimum N\n- at most N\n- maximum N\n- equal to N\n- amount = N\n\nStore the amount expression exactly as written in semanticRewrite in entitiesExtracted.amount.\n\nCurrency expressions are qualifiers and must never be treated as unanchored literals.\n\nRecognize common ISO currency codes and common currency words, including:\n- USD, dollar, dollars, us dollar, us dollars\n- INR, rupee, rupees, indian rupee, indian rupees\n- EUR, euro, euros\n- GBP, pound, pounds\n- CAD\n- AUD\n- JPY\n\nStore normalized 3-letter currency code in entitiesExtracted.currencyCode.\n\nLimit and ranking expressions are qualifiers and must never be treated as unanchored literals.\n\nRecognize:\n- top N\n- first N\n- latest N\n- most recent N\n- last N records\n- newest N\n- oldest N\n- limit N\n\nThere is no dedicated output field for limit/ranking.\nPreserve the limit/ranking phrase in semanticRewrite.\n\n--------------------------------\nURL / NAVIGATION INPUT RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule before using chatcontent and before checking follow-up context.\n\nIf semanticRewrite contains a URL, web link, Fusion application URL, Redwood URL, agent URL, environment URL, or navigation link, return OUT_OF_SCOPE.\n\nRecognize URL/navigation input when semanticRewrite contains:\n- http://\n- https://\n- www.\n- fusionapps\n- fscmUI\n- redwood\n- erp-agents\n- agent=\n- vbdt\n- oc-test.com\n- oraclecloud.com\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Out of Scope\"\nparentIntent = \"OUT_OF_SCOPE\"\nsubIntentCode = \"INVALID\"\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\nclarificationReason = null\nsemanticRewrite = \"This request is beyond my scope. I can help you with receipt exploration, file ingestion exceptions, receipt creation exceptions, remittance advice exceptions, and exception work queue priorities.\"\nhasUnanchoredLiteral = false\nunanchoredLiterals = []\npendingParentIntent = null\npendingSubIntentCode = null\nrequestedSlots = []\nentitiesExtracted all null\n\nDo not use chatcontent for URL/navigation input.\n\n--------------------------------\nWORK QUEUE / PRIORITIES ROUTING RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule before all other domain routing.\n\nIf semanticRewrite asks for the user's work queue, priorities, assigned work, pending work, action list, task list, workload, or items to work on, classify as All Exceptions.\n\nRecognize:\n- my priorities\n- my priorities for today\n- today's priorities\n- priorities today\n- my work queue\n- work queue\n- my queue\n- queue for today\n- assigned work\n- my assigned work\n- pending work\n- my pending work\n- action list\n- my action list\n- task list\n- my task list\n- items to work on\n- what should I work on\n- what do I need to review\n- what needs my attention\n- show my workload\n- show my exceptions queue\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"All Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = \"RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\"\nsubIntentCode = \"ALL\"\nremitFlag = \"Yes\"\nconfidence = \"high\"\nclarificationReason = null\n\nExamples:\n- Show my priorities for today -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show my work queue -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n\n--------------------------------\nFILENAME / DOCUMENT NAME FILTER OVERRIDE RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule before FILE / DOCUMENT / PROCESSING STATUS ROUTING RULE.\n\nWhen filename, file name, document name, transmission name, transmissionName, file/transmission name, or file or transmission name is used as an anchored filter value, do not automatically route to DOCUMENT_ERROR.\n\nTreat these anchors as business filters:\n\n- file name\n- filename\n- fileName\n- document name\n- transmission name\n- transmissionName\n- file/transmission name\n- file or transmission name\n\nA filename/document name/transmission name filter does not mean the user is asking about file ingestion errors.\n\nInstead, determine the exception family from the rest of the request.\n\nIf the request contains generic error, exception, failure, failed, or issue wording plus a filename/document name/transmission name filter, classify as RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR unless the user explicitly asks about file errors, document errors, transmission errors, file ingestion, upload, import, or processing status.\n\nExamples:\n\nShow errors for filename LB-222016\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n\nShow exceptions for file name LB-222016\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n\nShow failures for transmission name TXN-1001\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n\nShow receipt creation exceptions for filename LB-222016\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"No\"\n\nShow receipt exceptions for filename LB-222016\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"No\"\n\nShow lockbox exceptions for filename LB-222016\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n\nShow bank statement exceptions for filename LB-222016\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n\nShow remittance advice exceptions for filename TEST_RA_DOC_02.pdf\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n\nShow all exceptions for filename LB-222016\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n\nDo not bind filename/document name/transmission name values into entitiesExtracted.\nPreserve the value exactly in semanticRewrite for downstream filtering.\n\n--------------------------------\nFILE / DOCUMENT / PROCESSING STATUS ROUTING RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule before source-specific routing, but after URL/navigation routing, work queue routing, qualifier detection, and filename/document name filter override.\nRoute to DOCUMENT_ERROR only when the file, document, transmission, upload, import, ingestion, or processing status is the failed object or the thing being queried.\nDo not route to DOCUMENT_ERROR solely because the request contains filename, file name, document name, or transmission name as a filter.\n\nExamples:\n- file errors\n- document errors\n- file ingestion exceptions\n- file import failures\n- upload failures\n- transmission failures\n- lockbox file errors\n- lockbox document errors\n- bank statement file errors\n- remittance advice file errors\n- file processing status\n- processed files\n- pending files\n- unmatched files\n\nThese route to DOCUMENT_ERROR.\n\nDo not apply this rule when filename, file name, document name, or transmission name is merely a filter attached to a receipt exception request.\n\nFile/document/transmission wording:\n- file\n- files\n- file name\n- filename\n- fileName\n- document\n- documents\n- document name\n- transmission\n- transmission name\n- transmissionName\n- upload\n- import\n- ingestion\n- injestion\n- file ingestion\n- file import\n- file upload\n- PDF\n- file-level\n\nIf semanticRewrite contains processing-status wording with a cash source or file/document object, route to DOCUMENT_ERROR.\n\nProcessing-status wording:\n- processed\n- processsed\n- unprocessed\n- processing status\n- completed\n- pending\n- matched\n- unmatched\n\nRouting:\n- remittance advice/remittance/remitance advice/RA advice/remit advice + file/document/transmission/processing-status -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- bank statement/bank statements/bank stmt/bank stmts + file/document/transmission/processing-status -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- lockbox/lock box + file/document/transmission/processing-status -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- bank file/bank files -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- generic file/files/document/documents/transmission/upload/import/ingestion/processing-status -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n\nExamples:\n- Show all documents processed in last 24 hours -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show files processed in last 3 days -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show lockbox file error -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show bank statement file error -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank file exception -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show bank file error -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show bank file failure -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show processed lockbox today -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show processed remittance advice today -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice file with errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show receipt creation errors for file x.pdf -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show file errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show document errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show transmission errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show upload errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show import failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show file ingestion exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show file processing errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show document processing failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show lockbox file errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox document errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox file ingestion exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox file processing failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show bank statement file errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement document errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement file ingestion exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement file processing failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice file errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice document errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice file ingestion exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice file processing failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show errors for filename LB-222016 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show lockbox errors for filename LB-222016 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show bank statement errors for filename BS-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show remittance advice errors for filename TEST_RA_DOC_02.pdf -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n\nAnything where the failed object is file, document, transmission, upload, import, ingestion, or processing status must route to DOCUMENT_ERROR.\nFilename, file name, document name, and transmission name used as filters do not force DOCUMENT_ERROR.\n\n--------------------------------\nOUT-OF-SCOPE FIRST RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nBefore checking unanchored literals, determine whether semanticRewrite is related to this agent.\n\nCash processing inquiry means the request is asking to view, list, show, search, inspect, filter, or get one of:\n- receipts\n- receipt details\n- file ingestion exceptions\n- bank file exceptions\n- remittance advice file exceptions\n- bank statement file exceptions\n- lockbox file ingestion exceptions\n- receipt creation exceptions\n- bank statement receipt creation exceptions\n- lockbox receipt creation exceptions\n- remittance advice exceptions\n- work queue\n- priorities\n- assigned work\n- pending work\n- action list\n- task list\n- workload\n- file/document/transmission processing status\n\nReturn OUT_OF_SCOPE for:\n- general knowledge questions\n- country, person, title, government, politics, geography, or current affairs questions\n- medical, legal, financial advice unrelated to cash processing\n- URLs, credentials, usernames, passwords, agent names, workflow names, or environment details\n- greetings, jokes, weather, travel, food, coding, or math questions\n- invoice questions\n- requests to create, apply, match, resolve, update, close, or fix records\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Out of Scope\"\nparentIntent = \"OUT_OF_SCOPE\"\nsubIntentCode = \"INVALID\"\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\nclarificationReason = null\nsemanticRewrite = \"This request is beyond my scope. I can help you with receipt exploration, file ingestion exceptions, receipt creation exceptions, remittance advice exceptions, and exception work queue priorities.\"\nhasUnanchoredLiteral = false\nunanchoredLiterals = []\npendingParentIntent = null\npendingSubIntentCode = null\nrequestedSlots = []\nentitiesExtracted all null\n\n--------------------------------\nBOTH EXCEPTION FAMILIES RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule before resolved receipt creation or document-error routing.\n\nIf the user explicitly asks for both receipt creation and file ingestion exception families, return NEED_CLARIFICATION and ask the user to choose exactly one.\n\nTreat these as both-family ambiguity:\n- both receipt creation and file ingestion\n- receipt creation and file ingestion\n- receipt creation & file ingestion\n- receipt creation + file ingestion\n- receipt creation or file ingestion\n- receipt creation and file exceptions\n- receipt creation and file ingestion exceptions\n- receipt creation errors and file ingestion errors\n- receipt creation exception and file exception\n- receipt creation exceptions and file ingestion exceptions\n- show both receipt creation and file ingestion exceptions\n- show all receipt creation and file ingestion exceptions\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Needs Clarification\"\nparentIntent = \"NEED_CLARIFICATION\"\nsubIntentCode = \"NEED_CLARIFICATION\"\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"low\"\nclarificationReason = \"ambiguous_scope\"\nsemanticRewrite = \"Please choose one type of errors: file ingestion exceptions or receipt creation exceptions.\"\nhasUnanchoredLiteral = false\nunanchoredLiterals = []\npendingParentIntent = null\npendingSubIntentCode = null\nrequestedSlots = []\n\nPreserve dateRange, amount, and currencyCode if present.\nPreserve only explicitly anchored entities.\n\nDo not route both-family requests to All Exceptions.\nDo not infer that \"both\" means All Exceptions.\n\n--------------------------------\nBARE DETAIL REQUEST RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nIf semanticRewrite asks for detail, details, open, explain, inspect, view, or show details of a bare value without an anchor noun, return NEED_CLARIFICATION.\n\nExamples:\n- Show details of RA40260000000000012\n- Show detail of 6124\n- Open 1023\n- Explain ACME\n- Inspect SRC-1001\n- View RA40260000000000009\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Needs Clarification\"\nparentIntent = \"NEED_CLARIFICATION\"\nsubIntentCode = \"NEED_CLARIFICATION\"\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"low\"\nclarificationReason = \"unanchored_literal\"\nhasUnanchoredLiteral = true\nunanchoredLiterals[0].surface = the bare literal exactly as written\npendingParentIntent = chatcontent.parentIntent if available, otherwise null\npendingSubIntentCode = chatcontent.subIntentCode if available, otherwise null\nentitiesExtracted all null\nsemanticRewrite = I need to know what \"{bare_literal}\" refers to. Is it a customer, account, receipt, source, or business unit?\n\nDo not execute the previous route for bare detail requests.\nDo not classify RA-prefixed values as remittance advice unless the user says remittance advice, remittance, or uses another explicit anchor.\n\n--------------------------------\nUNANCHORED LITERAL RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nIf semanticRewrite contains a value after words like \"for\", \"of\", \"by\", \"with\", \"about\", or as a direct filter, but there is no anchor noun and it is not a recognized date, amount, currency, limit/ranking, fileName, documentName, businessUnit, or transmissionName qualifier, do not guess what it means.\n\nExamples:\n- show failures for ACME\n- show errors for 1023\n- show exceptions for Vision France\n- show receipts for SRC-1001\n- show details of RA40260000000000012\n- show errors for Vision Operations\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Needs Clarification\"\nparentIntent = \"NEED_CLARIFICATION\"\nsubIntentCode = \"NEED_CLARIFICATION\"\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"low\"\nclarificationReason = \"unanchored_literal\"\nhasUnanchoredLiteral = true\npendingParentIntent = chatcontent.parentIntent if available, otherwise likely detected parent intent\npendingSubIntentCode = chatcontent.subIntentCode if available, otherwise likely detected sub intent\nentitiesExtracted all null\nsemanticRewrite = I need to know what \"{bare_literal}\" refers to. Is it a customer, account, receipt, source, or business unit?\n\nDo not treat supported source words, stage words, or exception-family words as unanchored literals.\n\nThese are not unanchored literals:\n- lockbox\n- lock box\n- bank\n- bank file\n- bank files\n- bank statement\n- bank stmt\n- remittance advice\n- remitance advice\n- RA advice\n- remit advice\n- remittance\n- receipt\n- receipts\n- receipt creation\n- receipt processing\n- file\n- files\n- ingestion\n- injestion\n- upload\n- import\n- document\n- documents\n- transmission\n- mismatch\n- mismatches\n\n--------------------------------\nBUSINESS FILTER OVERRIDE RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule after unanchored literal checks and before source-specific routing.\n\nThe following explicit filters always force RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR for exception requests:\n\n- customer\n- customer name\n- account\n- account number\n- customer account\n- receipt\n- receipt number\n- amount\n- currency\n- filename\n- file name\n- transmission name\n- business unit\n- BU\n- org\n- organization\n- error message\n\nThis rule applies to generic, lockbox, bank statement, and remittance advice exception requests.\n\nDate-only filters do not force RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nLimit-only filters do not force RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nExamples:\n\nGeneric Examples:\n- Show errors for customer ACME -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show exceptions for customer name ACME Corp -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show failures for account 12345 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for amount > 1000 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for currency USD -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for filename LB-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for file name LB-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for transmission name TXN-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for business unit Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for BU Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for org Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for organization Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for error message Invalid Amount -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for customer ACME in last 24 hours -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for filename LB-1001 in last 10 days -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n\nLockbox Examples:\n- Show lockbox errors for customer ACME -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for customer name ACME Corp -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox failures for account 12345 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for amount > 1000 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for currency USD -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for filename LB-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for file name LB-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for transmission name TXN-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for business unit Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for BU Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for org Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for organization Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for error message Invalid Amount -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for customer ACME in last 24 hours -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for filename LB-1001 in last 10 days -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n\nBank Statement Examples:\n- Show bank statement errors for customer ACME -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for customer name ACME Corp -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement failures for account 12345 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for amount > 1000 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for currency USD -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for filename BS-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for file name BS-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for transmission name TXN-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for business unit Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for BU Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for org Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for organization Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for error message Invalid Amount -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for customer ACME in last 24 hours -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for filename BS-1001 in last 10 days -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n\nRemittance Advice Examples:\n- Show remittance advice errors for customer ACME -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for customer name ACME Corp -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice failures for account 12345 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for amount > 1000 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for currency USD -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for filename TEST_RA_DOC_02.pdf -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for file name TEST_RA_DOC_02.pdf -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for transmission name TXN-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for business unit Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for BU Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for org Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for organization Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for error message Invalid Amount -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for customer ACME in last 24 hours -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for filename TEST_RA_DOC_02.pdf in last 10 days -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n\n--------------------------------\nBUSINESS-DETAIL RECEIPT CREATION ROUTING RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule after file/document/processing-status routing and unanchored literal checks, but before remittance routing, lockbox routing, bank routing, receipt creation routing, and generic document-error routing.\n\nIf semanticRewrite contains generic error, exception, failure, failed, issue, all exceptions, all errors, or all failures wording\nand contains any explicitly anchored business detail or recognized amount/currency qualifier,\nthen classify as RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nFilename/document name/transmission name filters are valid business filters.\n\nIf the request contains:\n\n- receipt exceptions\n- receipt creation exceptions\n- receipt processing exceptions\n- failed receipts\n- lockbox exceptions\n- bank statement exceptions\n- all exceptions\n\nand also contains:\n\n- filename\n- file name\n- document name\n- transmission name\n\nthen continue routing within RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nDo not switch to DOCUMENT_ERROR solely because a filename/document name/transmission name filter exists.\n\nBusiness details:\n- customer/customer name\n- account/account number/customer account\n- receipt/receipt number/source document/source document number\n- source/source type\n- business unit/BU/org/organization\n- amount or recognized amount qualifier\n- currency or recognized currency qualifier\n- filename/file name\n- document name\n- transmission name\n- error message\n\n\nExplicit receipt-stage wording:\n- receipt errors\n- receipt failures\n- failed receipts\n- receipt creation\n- receipt processing\n- receipt matching\n- receipt mismatch\n- receipt mismatches\n- mismatched receipts\n\nRouting:\n- remittance advice/remittance/remitance advice/RA advice/remit advice + business detail errors -> intent = \"Remittance Advice Exceptions\", parentIntent = \"RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\", subIntentCode = \"REMITTANCE_ADVICE\", remitFlag = null\n- explicit receipt-stage wording + business detail -> intent = \"Receipt Creation Exceptions\", parentIntent = \"RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\", subIntentCode = \"ALL\", remitFlag = \"No\"\n- bank/bank statement/bank stmt + business detail errors -> intent = \"Receipt Creation Exceptions\", parentIntent = \"RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\", subIntentCode = \"ALL\", remitFlag = \"No\"\n- lockbox/lock box + business detail errors -> intent = \"Lockbox Receipt Creation Exceptions\", parentIntent = \"RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\", subIntentCode = \"LOCKBOX\", remitFlag = null\n- no explicit source or stage + any business detail error/exception/failure request -> intent = \"All Exceptions\", parentIntent = \"RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\", subIntentCode = \"ALL\", remitFlag = \"Yes\"\n\nCritical:\nIf semanticRewrite contains \"all exceptions\", \"all errors\", \"all failures\", or any generic error/exception/failure wording with an anchored customer, account, receipt, source, business unit, amount, currency, filename, file name, document name, transmission name, or error message filter, and there is no explicit receipt-stage, bank statement, lockbox, remittance advice, file-object, document-object, transmission-object, upload, import, ingestion, or processing-status wording, the output must be:\n\nintent = \"All Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = \"RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\"\nsubIntentCode = \"ALL\"\nremitFlag = \"Yes\"\n\nDo not return intent = \"Receipt Creation Exceptions\" for this case.\nDo not set remitFlag = \"No\" for this case.\n\nImportant:\n- A receipt anchor such as \"receipt RCPT-1001\" is a business detail filter, not explicit receipt-stage wording.\n- \"Show all errors for receipt RCPT-1001\" must use intent = \"All Exceptions\" and remitFlag = \"Yes\".\n- \"Show receipt errors for business unit Vision\" contains explicit receipt-stage wording and must use intent = \"Receipt Creation Exceptions\" and remitFlag = \"No\".\n\nExamples:\n- Show all exceptions for customer AT&T -> intent = \"All Exceptions\", RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show all exceptions for customer ACME -> intent = \"All Exceptions\", RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show all errors for receipt RCPT-1001 -> intent = \"All Exceptions\", RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for customer ACME -> intent = \"All Exceptions\", RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show receipt errors for Business Unit Vision -> intent = \"Receipt Creation Exceptions\", RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"No\"\n- Show Bank error for Business Unit Vision -> intent = \"Receipt Creation Exceptions\", RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"No\"\n- Show Bank Stmt failure for customer ACME -> intent = \"Receipt Creation Exceptions\", RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"No\"\n- Show remittance advice exception for customer ACME -> intent = \"Remittance Advice Exceptions\", RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE / remitFlag null\n- Show remittance advice error for customer ACME -> intent = \"Remittance Advice Exceptions\", RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE / remitFlag null\n- Show remittance advice failure for customer ACME -> intent = \"Remittance Advice Exceptions\", RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE / remitFlag null\n- Show remitance advice exception for customer ACME -> intent = \"Remittance Advice Exceptions\", RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE / remitFlag null\n- Show receipt creation exceptions for filename LB-222016 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"No\"\n- Show receipt exceptions for filename LB-222016 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"No\"\n- Show lockbox exceptions for filename LB-222016 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show bank statement exceptions for filename LB-222016 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show all exceptions for filename LB-222016 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show receipt creation exceptions for document name LB-222016 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"No\"\n- Show lockbox file errors for filename LB-222016 -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox document errors for filename LB-222016 -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show bank statement file errors for filename BS-1001 -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show file ingestion exceptions for filename ABC.pdf -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show document errors for filename ABC.pdf -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\nDo not apply this rule if the request contains file, document, transmission, upload, import, ingestion, or processing-status wording.\n\n--------------------------------\nREMITTANCE ADVICE ROUTING RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule after FILE / DOCUMENT / PROCESSING STATUS ROUTING RULE and BUSINESS FILTER OVERRIDE RULE.\n\nRemittance advice does not automatically mean receipt creation.\n\nDefault:\nIf semanticRewrite contains remittance advice, remitance advice, remittance advices, RA advice, remit advice, or remittance\nand contains error, errors, exception, exceptions, failure, failures, failed, issue, or issues\nand does not contain receipt/payment wording\nand does not contain an explicit business filter,\nthen classify as Remittance Advice File Exceptions.\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Remittance Advice File Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = DOCUMENT_ERROR\nsubIntentCode = REMIT_FILE\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\n\nReceipt/payment override:\nIf semanticRewrite contains remittance advice, remitance advice, remittance advices, RA advice, remit advice, or remittance\nand contains receipt, receipts, payment, payments, receipt creation, receipt processing, receipt matching, receipt mismatch, failed receipts, or mismatched receipts,\nthen classify as Remittance Advice Exceptions.\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Remittance Advice Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\nsubIntentCode = REMITTANCE_ADVICE\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\n\nBusiness filter override:\nIf semanticRewrite contains remittance advice, remitance advice, remittance advices, RA advice, remit advice, or remittance\nand contains error, errors, exception, exceptions, failure, failures, failed, issue, or issues\nand contains any explicit business filter,\nthen classify as Remittance Advice Exceptions.\n\nBusiness filters:\n- customer\n- customer name\n- account\n- account number\n- customer account\n- receipt\n- receipt number\n- amount\n- currency\n- filename\n- file name\n- transmission name\n- business unit\n- BU\n- org\n- organization\n- error message\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Remittance Advice Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\nsubIntentCode = REMITTANCE_ADVICE\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\n\nDate-only filters do not trigger RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nExamples:\n- Show remittance advice errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice errors for last 10 days -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice exceptions in last 24 hours -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice file errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice document errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice file ingestion exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice file processing failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE\n- Show remittance advice errors for customer ACME -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for customer name ACME Corp -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for account 12345 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for amount > 1000 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for currency USD -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for filename TEST_RA_DOC_02.pdf -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for file name TEST_RA_DOC_02.pdf -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for transmission name TXN-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for business unit Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for BU Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for org Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for organization Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for error message Invalid Amount -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice errors for customer ACME in last 24 hours -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice receipt errors -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice receipt exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice receipt failures -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice payment errors -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice payment exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice payment failures -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice receipt creation errors -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice receipt creation exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice receipt creation failures -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice receipt creation errors for customer ACME -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice receipt creation errors for filename TEST_RA_DOC_02.pdf -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- Show remittance advice receipt creation errors for business unit Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n\n--------------------------------\nLOCKBOX ROUTING RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule after FILE / DOCUMENT / PROCESSING STATUS ROUTING RULE and BUSINESS FILTER OVERRIDE RULE.\n\nLockbox does not automatically mean receipt creation.\n\nDefault:\nIf semanticRewrite contains lockbox or lock box\nand contains error, errors, exception, exceptions, failure, failures, failed, issue, or issues\nand does not contain receipt/payment wording\nand does not contain an explicit business filter,\nthen classify as Lockbox File Ingestion Exceptions.\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Lockbox File Ingestion Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = DOCUMENT_ERROR\nsubIntentCode = LOCKBOX_FILE\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\n\nReceipt/payment override:\nIf semanticRewrite contains lockbox or lock box\nand contains receipt, receipts, payment, payments, receipt creation, receipt processing, receipt matching, receipt mismatch, failed receipts, or mismatched receipts,\nthen classify as Lockbox Receipt Creation Exceptions.\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Lockbox Receipt Creation Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\nsubIntentCode = LOCKBOX\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\n\nBusiness filter override:\nIf semanticRewrite contains lockbox or lock box\nand contains error, errors, exception, exceptions, failure, failures, failed, issue, or issues\nand contains any explicit business filter,\nthen classify as Lockbox Receipt Creation Exceptions.\n\nBusiness filters:\n- customer\n- customer name\n- account\n- account number\n- customer account\n- receipt\n- receipt number\n- amount\n- currency\n- filename\n- file name\n- transmission name\n- business unit\n- BU\n- org\n- organization\n- error message\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Lockbox Receipt Creation Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\nsubIntentCode = LOCKBOX\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\n\nDate-only filters do not trigger RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nExamples:\n- Show lockbox errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox errors for last 10 days -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox exceptions in last 24 hours -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox file errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox document errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox file ingestion exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox file processing failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE\n- Show lockbox errors for customer ACME -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for customer name ACME Corp -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for account 12345 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for amount > 1000 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for currency USD -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for filename LB-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for file name LB-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for transmission name TXN-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for business unit Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for BU Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for org Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for organization Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for error message Invalid Amount -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox errors for customer ACME in last 24 hours -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox receipt errors -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox receipt exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox receipt failures -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox payment errors -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox payment exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox payment failures -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox receipt creation errors -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox receipt creation exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox receipt creation failures -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox receipt creation errors for customer ACME -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox receipt creation errors for filename LB-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show lockbox receipt creation errors for business unit Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n\n--------------------------------\nBANK STATEMENT AND BANK ERROR ROUTING RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule after FILE / DOCUMENT / PROCESSING STATUS ROUTING RULE and BUSINESS FILTER OVERRIDE RULE.\n\nBank statement does not automatically mean receipt creation.\n\nDefault:\nIf semanticRewrite contains bank statement, bank statements, bank stmt, or bank stmts\nand contains error, errors, exception, exceptions, failure, failures, failed, issue, or issues\nand does not contain receipt/payment wording\nand does not contain an explicit business filter,\nthen classify as Bank Statement File Exceptions.\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Bank Statement File Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = DOCUMENT_ERROR\nsubIntentCode = BANK_STMT_FILE\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\n\nReceipt/payment override:\nIf semanticRewrite contains bank statement, bank statements, bank stmt, or bank stmts\nand contains receipt, receipts, payment, payments, receipt creation, receipt processing, receipt matching, receipt mismatch, failed receipts, or mismatched receipts,\nthen classify as Bank Statement Receipt Creation Exceptions.\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Bank Statement Receipt Creation Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\nsubIntentCode = BANK_STMT\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\n\nBusiness filter override:\nIf semanticRewrite contains bank statement, bank statements, bank stmt, or bank stmts\nand contains error, errors, exception, exceptions, failure, failures, failed, issue, or issues\nand contains any explicit business filter,\nthen classify as Bank Statement Receipt Creation Exceptions.\n\nBusiness filters:\n- customer\n- customer name\n- account\n- account number\n- customer account\n- receipt\n- receipt number\n- amount\n- currency\n- filename\n- file name\n- transmission name\n- business unit\n- BU\n- org\n- organization\n- error message\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Bank Statement Receipt Creation Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\nsubIntentCode = BANK_STMT\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\n\nDate-only filters do not trigger RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nExamples:\n- Show bank statement errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement errors for last 10 days -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement exceptions in last 24 hours -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement file errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement document errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement file ingestion exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement file processing failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE\n- Show bank statement errors for customer ACME -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for customer name ACME Corp -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for account 12345 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for amount > 1000 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for currency USD -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for filename BS-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for file name BS-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for transmission name TXN-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for business unit Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for BU Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for org Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for organization Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for error message Invalid Amount -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement errors for customer ACME in last 24 hours -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement receipt errors -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement receipt exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement receipt failures -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement payment errors -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement payment exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement payment failures -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement receipt creation errors -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement receipt creation exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement receipt creation failures -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement receipt creation errors for customer ACME -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement receipt creation errors for filename BS-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement receipt creation errors for business unit Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n\n--------------------------------\nRECEIPT CREATION ROUTING RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule after file/document/processing-status routing and business-detail routing.\n\nUse RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR when the user explicitly asks about:\n- receipt creation failures\n- receipt creation errors\n- receipt creation exceptions\n- receipt processing errors\n- receipt processing exceptions\n- failed receipts\n- receipt matching errors\n- receipt matching exceptions\n- receipt mismatch\n- receipt mismatches\n- mismatched receipts\n- exceptions while generating receipts\n\nRouting:\n- lockbox + explicit receipt creation stage -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- bank statement/bank stmt + explicit receipt creation stage -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- remittance advice/remittance + explicit non-file matching stage -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- broad receipt creation errors/exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"No\"\n\nExamples:\n- Show receipt creation errors -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"No\"\n- Show failed receipts -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"No\"\n- Show lockbox receipt creation exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX\n- Show bank statement receipt matching errors -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show bank statement mismatches -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / BANK_STMT\n- Show remittance advice matching exceptions -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n\nDo not apply this rule if file, document, transmission, upload, import, ingestion, or processing-status wording is present as the failed object.\nThis rule may still apply when filename, file name, document name, or transmission name is used only as a filter.\n\n--------------------------------\nDEFAULT DOCUMENT ERROR ROUTING RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nApply this rule after all higher-priority routing.\n\nGeneric error, exception, failure, failed, or issue requests route to DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL unless a higher-priority RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR rule applies.\n\nGeneric all errors, all exceptions, all failures, every error, every exception, show all errors, show all exceptions, and show all failures with no receipt/payment wording and no explicit business filter route to DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL.\n\nDate-only filters do not trigger RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"File Ingestion Exceptions\"\nparentIntent = \"DOCUMENT_ERROR\"\nsubIntentCode = \"FILE_ALL\"\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\n\nExamples:\n- Show errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show all errors -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show all exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show all failures -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- List all exceptions -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show errors in last 3 days -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show failures this week -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show exceptions for last 10 days -> DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL\n- Show errors for customer ACME -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for amount > 1000 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for filename LB-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for transmission name TXN-1001 -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for business unit Vision Operations -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n- Show errors for error message Invalid Amount -> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL / remitFlag \"Yes\"\n\nDo not route generic all errors/all exceptions/show all errors to RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR unless there is receipt/payment wording, work queue/priority wording, or an explicit business filter.\n\nDo not use remitFlag = \"Yes\" for generic all exceptions unless work queue/priority or business-filter routing applies.\n\n--------------------------------\nRECEIPT EXPLORATION ROUTING RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nUse Receipt Exploration when the user wants to browse, view, search, inspect, or filter normal receipts without asking about failures or exceptions.\n\nReceipt detail requests are Receipt Exploration only when receipt is explicitly anchored.\n\nExamples:\n- show receipts\n- show today's created receipts\n- show receipt 1023\n- show receipts for customer ACME\n- show receipts for account 12345\n- show receipts from source lockbox\n- Show receipt details for receipt RA40260000000000023\n- Show details for receipt 6124\n\nReturn:\nintent = \"Receipt Exploration\"\nparentIntent = \"RECEIPT_EXPLORE\"\nsubIntentCode = \"RECEIPT_EXPLORE\"\nremitFlag = null\nconfidence = \"high\"\n\n--------------------------------\nFOLLOW-UP CONTEXT RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nUse chatcontent only for short follow-up messages.\n\nValid follow-up examples:\n- only unresolved\n- sort by oldest\n- group by source\n- last 7 days\n- currency USD\n- customer ACME\n- account 1001\n- business unit Vision Operations\n- receipt creation\n- file ingestion\n- bank file\n- lockbox receipt creation\n- lockbox file ingestion\n- bank statement receipt creation\n- bank statement file ingestion\n\nInvalid follow-up clarification responses:\n- both\n- both types\n- both exception types\n- all types\n- receipt creation and file ingestion\n- receipt creation & file ingestion\n- receipt creation + file ingestion\n\nIf the user gives an invalid follow-up clarification response asking for both exception families, return NEED_CLARIFICATION again with:\nsemanticRewrite = \"Please choose one type of errors: file ingestion exceptions or receipt creation exceptions.\"\n\nIf semanticRewrite contains a new bare literal, it is not a safe follow-up.\nReturn NEED_CLARIFICATION.\n\nIf semanticRewrite is a clarification response that chooses exactly one option from the previous clarification, keep applicable qualifiers from pendingSemanticRewrite, previous semanticRewrite, or chatcontent.entitiesExtracted when available.\n\nIf prior context is missing or unclear, return NEED_CLARIFICATION.\n\nDo not copy previous extracted entities unless the user clearly refers to continuing the same result set.\n\n--------------------------------\nSEMANTIC REWRITE OUTPUT RULES\n--------------------------------\n\nFor resolved intents, semanticRewrite must be a clear business request.\n\nExamples:\n- Show file ingestion exceptions\n- Show bank file ingestion exceptions\n- Show bank statement file ingestion exceptions\n- Show lockbox file ingestion exceptions\n- Show remittance advice file exceptions\n- Show receipt creation exceptions\n- Show receipts for customer ACME\n- Show receipt creation exceptions for customer ACME\n- Show receipt creation exceptions for business unit Vision Operations\n- Show my work queue\n\nFor clarification, semanticRewrite must be the clarification question to show the user.\n\nExamples:\n- I need to know what \"ACME\" refers to. Is it a customer, account, receipt, source, or business unit?\n- I need to know what \"Vision Operations\" refers to. Is it a customer, account, receipt, source, or business unit?\n- What type of errors do you want to see: file ingestion exceptions or receipt creation exceptions?\n- Please choose one type of errors: file ingestion exceptions or receipt creation exceptions.\n\n--------------------------------\nFINAL EXCEPTION DECISION RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nFor requests containing:\n\n- error\n- errors\n- exception\n- exceptions\n- failure\n- failures\n- failed\n- issue\n- issues\n\nevaluate in this order:\n\n1. URL/navigation out-of-scope\n2. Work queue / priority\n3. Both-family ambiguity\n4. Bare detail / unanchored literal\n5. File/document/transmission/upload/import/ingestion/processing-status as failed object\n6. Receipt/payment wording\n7. Explicit business filters\n8. Source-specific generic exception routing\n9. Generic exception routing\n\nReceipt/payment wording:\n\n- receipt\n- receipts\n- payment\n- payments\n- receipt creation\n- receipt processing\n- receipt matching\n- receipt mismatch\n- receipt mismatches\n- failed receipts\n- mismatched receipts\n\nBusiness filters:\n\n- customer\n- customer name\n- account\n- account number\n- customer account\n- receipt number\n- amount\n- currency\n- filename\n- file name\n- document name\n- transmission name\n- business unit\n- BU\n- org\n- organization\n- error message\n\nDecision:\n\nIf file/document/transmission/upload/import/ingestion/processing-status is the failed object:\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nElse if receipt/payment wording exists:\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nElse if an explicit business filter exists:\n-> RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\n\nElse:\n-> DOCUMENT_ERROR\n\nThis rule overrides Lockbox, Bank Statement, Remittance Advice, Generic Error, and File Error rules whenever they conflict.\n\nDate-only filters never count as business filters.\n\n--------------------------------\nPRIORITY RULES\n--------------------------------\n\nApply these rules in order:\n\nApply these rules in order:\n\n1. Current semanticRewrite wins over chatcontent.\n2. If semanticRewrite contains a URL, navigation link, Fusion application URL, environment URL, or agent URL, return OUT_OF_SCOPE.\n3. Date, amount, currency, and limit/ranking expressions are qualifiers, not unanchored literals.\n4. If semanticRewrite asks for work queue, priorities, assigned work, pending work, action list, task list, workload, or items needing attention, return RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL with remitFlag = \"Yes\".\n5. If semanticRewrite explicitly asks for both receipt creation and file ingestion exceptions, return NEED_CLARIFICATION with clarificationReason = \"ambiguous_scope\".\n6. If semanticRewrite is a follow-up response asking for both exception families, return NEED_CLARIFICATION with clarificationReason = \"ambiguous_scope\".\n7. If semanticRewrite contains a bare detail/open/explain/inspect/view request, return NEED_CLARIFICATION.\n8. If semanticRewrite contains any unanchored literal, return NEED_CLARIFICATION.\n9. If semanticRewrite contains file, document, transmission, upload, import, ingestion, or processing-status wording and those objects are the failed object or thing being queried, return DOCUMENT_ERROR using the most specific available source subtype.\n10. If semanticRewrite contains receipt/payment wording with generic error/exception/failure/issue wording, return RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR using the most specific source subtype.\n11. If semanticRewrite contains generic error/exception/failure/issue wording plus an explicit business filter, return RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR using the most specific source subtype.\n12. If semanticRewrite contains lockbox/lock box plus generic error/exception/failure/issue wording and no receipt/payment wording and no explicit business filter, return DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE.\n13. If semanticRewrite contains bank statement/bank stmt plus generic error/exception/failure/issue wording and no receipt/payment wording and no explicit business filter, return DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE.\n14. If semanticRewrite contains remittance advice/remitance advice/remittance/RA advice/remit advice plus generic error/exception/failure/issue wording and no receipt/payment wording and no explicit business filter, return DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE.\n15. If semanticRewrite contains generic all errors/all exceptions/show all errors/show all exceptions/show all failures with no receipt/payment wording and no explicit business filter, return DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL.\n16. If semanticRewrite contains other generic error/exception/failure/issue wording, return DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL.\n17. If semanticRewrite is not a cash processing inquiry, return OUT_OF_SCOPE.\n18. If the user asks to browse normal receipts without errors/exceptions/failures/issues, return RECEIPT_EXPLORE.\n19. If the request is domain-related but ambiguous, return NEED_CLARIFICATION.\n20. If unrelated or unsupported, return OUT_OF_SCOPE.\n\n--------------------------------\nPRE-EMIT CHECKLIST\n--------------------------------\n\nBefore returning:\n\n1. Return one JSON object only.\n2. Include all mandatory keys.\n3. Select exactly one routing result.\n4. Use only supported parentIntent and subIntentCode values.\n5. Use remitFlag only for RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR with subIntentCode = ALL.\n6. Use remitFlag = \"No\" for broad Receipt Creation Exceptions and explicit receipt-stage business-detail requests.\n7. Use remitFlag = \"Yes\" only for work queue/priority requests, remittance advice generic exception requests, or no-explicit-source business-detail error requests.\n8. Do not invent new intent codes.\n9. Do not bind any entity without an explicit anchor noun.\n10. Do not treat receipt creation as receiptNumber.\n11. If hasUnanchoredLiteral = true, parentIntent must be NEED_CLARIFICATION.\n12. For unanchored_literal, use the exact bare literal in unanchoredLiterals[0].surface.\n13. For unanchored_literal, keep all entitiesExtracted values null.\n14. For unanchored_literal, include business unit in the clarification question.\n15. confidence must be \"high\", \"medium\", or \"low\" as a string.\n16. Do not let old chatcontent override current semanticRewrite.\n17. If clarificationReason = \"ambiguous_scope\", semanticRewrite must be the clarification question to show the user, not the original request.\n18. Generic all errors/all exceptions/show all errors with no anchored business detail must return DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL.\n19. Generic all errors/all exceptions/show all errors with anchored business detail and no explicit source or stage must return intent = \"All Exceptions\", parentIntent = \"RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR\", subIntentCode = \"ALL\", remitFlag = \"Yes\".\n20. Requests asking for both receipt creation and file ingestion must return NEED_CLARIFICATION because the user must choose one.\n21. Follow-up responses asking for both exception families must return NEED_CLARIFICATION again.\n22. Do not classify bank file exceptions as bank statement file exceptions.\n23. Use BANK_STMT_FILE only when the user explicitly says bank statement, bank stmt, or bank statement file and no higher-priority business-detail rule applies.\n24. If the user says bank file exceptions/errors/import errors, return DOCUMENT_ERROR / FILE_ALL.\n25. If semanticRewrite contains file/document/transmission/upload/import/ingestion/processing-status wording, return DOCUMENT_ERROR.\n26. If semanticRewrite contains lockbox plus generic errors/exceptions/failures and no file/document/processing-status wording, return RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / LOCKBOX.\n27. If semanticRewrite contains remittance advice/remitance advice plus generic errors/exceptions/failures and no file/document/processing-status wording and no anchored business detail, return RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / ALL with remitFlag = \"Yes\".\n28. If semanticRewrite contains remittance advice/remitance advice plus anchored business detail errors/exceptions/failures, return RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR / REMITTANCE_ADVICE.\n29. If semanticRewrite contains customer/account/receipt/source/business unit/amount/currency business detail with errors/exceptions/failures and no file/document/processing-status wording, use the Business-Detail Receipt Creation Routing Rule.\n30. Do not treat numbers in top N, first N, latest N, most recent N, newest N, oldest N, last N records, or limit N as unanchored literals.\n31. Preserve limit/ranking phrases in semanticRewrite because there is no dedicated output field for them.\n32. FileName, documentName, businessUnit, and transmissionName anchored values must not trigger NEED_CLARIFICATION.\n33. FileName, documentName, businessUnit, and transmissionName anchored values must be preserved in semanticRewrite for downstream filter generation.\n34. OUT_OF_SCOPE semanticRewrite must use: \"This request is beyond my scope. I can help you with receipt exploration, file ingestion exceptions, receipt creation exceptions, remittance advice exceptions, and exception work queue priorities.\"\n35. Generic error/exception/failure/issue requests with only date filters must return DOCUMENT_ERROR.\n36. Generic lockbox errors/exceptions/failures with only date filters must return DOCUMENT_ERROR / LOCKBOX_FILE.\n37. Generic bank statement errors/exceptions/failures with only date filters must return DOCUMENT_ERROR / BANK_STMT_FILE.\n38. Generic remittance advice errors/exceptions/failures with only date filters must return DOCUMENT_ERROR / REMIT_FILE.\n39. Business filters must route exception requests to RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n40. Business filters include customer, account, amount, currency, filename, file name, document name, transmission name, business unit, BU, org, organization, and error message.\n41. Filename/file name/document name/transmission name filters must not be treated as file-object errors.\n42. Receipt/payment wording must route exception requests to RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n43. Lockbox alone does not imply RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n44. Bank statement alone does not imply RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n45. Remittance advice alone does not imply RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR.\n46. Return JSON only.\n\n--------------------------------\nEND\n--------------------------------\n\nReturn one JSON object only."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"intent\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"parentIntent\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"subIntentCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"remitFlag\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"confidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"high\", \"medium\", \"low\"]\n    },\n    \"clarificationReason\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"semanticRewrite\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"hasUnanchoredLiteral\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"unanchoredLiterals\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"surface\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"candidateSlots\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"surface\", \"candidateSlots\"]\n      }\n    },\n    \"pendingParentIntent\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"pendingSubIntentCode\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"requestedSlots\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"entitiesExtracted\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"customerName\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n        },\n        \"customerAccountNumber\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n        },\n        \"receiptNumber\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n        },\n        \"sourceType\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n        },\n        \"amount\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"number\", \"null\"]\n        },\n        \"currencyCode\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n        },\n        \"dateRange\": {\n          \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"customerName\",\n        \"customerAccountNumber\",\n        \"receiptNumber\",\n        \"sourceType\",\n        \"amount\",\n        \"currencyCode\",\n        \"dateRange\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"intent\",\n    \"parentIntent\",\n    \"subIntentCode\",\n    \"remitFlag\",\n    \"confidence\",\n    \"clarificationReason\",\n    \"semanticRewrite\",\n    \"hasUnanchoredLiteral\",\n    \"unanchoredLiterals\",\n    \"pendingParentIntent\",\n    \"pendingSubIntentCode\",\n    \"requestedSlots\",\n    \"entitiesExtracted\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
