          "code": "DOCUMENTEXCEPTIONINQUIRY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1779170075323",
          "id": "1779097317979",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780947657262_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.semanticrewrite}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"output\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"null\"\n    },\n    \"followUpQuestions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"jobId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"conversationId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"traceId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"supportingChunks\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"citations\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"nodes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"waitingToolCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"null\"\n    },\n    \"workflowCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"workflowVersion\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"workflowStatus\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"startDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"endTime\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"createDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"endDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"timeTaken\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"inputTokenCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"outputTokenCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": []\n}",
          "type": "WORKFLOW"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Filter Generator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777039918702"
          },
          "code": "FILTER_GENERATOR",
          "id": "1777039515926",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777039515927_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a filter-construction engine for a Cash Processing Errors and Exceptions Inquiry agent.\n\nsemanticRewrite:\n{{$context.$variables.semanticrewrite}}\n\nchatcontent:\n{{$context.$variables.chatcontent}}\n\nUserParentIntent:\n{{$context.$variables.UserParentIntent}}\n\nUserIntent:\n{{$context.$variables.UserIntent}}\n\nYour job is to read semanticRewrite and return exactly one JSON object with this shape:\n\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \"\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nReturn only JSON.\nDo not explain anything.\nDo not add markdown.\nDo not add extra keys.\nDo not ask questions.\n\n--------------------------------\nPRIMARY INPUT RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nUse semanticRewrite as the primary and authoritative text for filter extraction.\n\nDo not use {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} for filter extraction.\n\nReason:\nRaw user input may be a short follow-up such as:\n- lockbox receipt creation\n- receipt\n- last 7 days\n- customer ACME\n\nsemanticRewrite is the resolved business request and may contain filters carried forward from prior clarification turns.\n\nExample:\nRaw user input:\nlockbox receipt creation\n\nsemanticRewrite:\nShow lockbox receipt creation exceptions last 12 days\n\nUse semanticRewrite and return:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND timeCreated > sysdate - 12 ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"LOCKBOX\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\n--------------------------------\nSTRUCTURED FALLBACK RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nUse chatcontent only as a fallback when semanticRewrite does not clearly contain a value.\n\nFallback fields:\n- chatcontent.entitiesExtracted.dateRange\n- chatcontent.entitiesExtracted.amount\n- chatcontent.entitiesExtracted.currencyCode\n- chatcontent.entitiesExtracted.customerName\n- chatcontent.sourceType if present\n- chatcontent.remitFlag if present\n- chatcontent.subIntentCode\n- chatcontent.parentIntent\n\nDo not let chatcontent override an explicit value in semanticRewrite.\n\n--------------------------------\nOUTPUT FIELDS\n--------------------------------\n\n1. filterClause\n- string containing SQL-like filter fragments\n- each condition must start with a leading space and AND\n- ORDER BY and FETCH FIRST clauses must be appended at the end\n- if no filter is found, return ORDER BY and FETCH FIRST defaults only\n\n2. sourceType\nAllowed values:\n- \"LOCKBOX\"\n- \"BANK_STATEMENT\"\n- \"REMITTANCE_ADVICE\"\n- \"ALL\"\n\n3. remitFlag\nAllowed values:\n- \"yes\"\n- \"no\"\n\n\"yes\" means remittance advice exceptions should be included.\n\"no\" means remittance advice exceptions should not be included.\n\n--------------------------------\nCOLUMN NAMES\n--------------------------------\n\nUse only these exact column names in filterClause:\n\n- timeCreated\n- amount\n- currencyCode\n- customerName\n- messageText\n- receiptDate\n- receiptNumber\n- fileName\n- transmissionName\n- businessUnitName\n\nDo not use any other column names.\n\n--------------------------------\nDO NOT FILTER ON INTENT / ROUTING WORDING\n--------------------------------\n\nDo not create messageText filters from intent, source, stage, or routing words.\n\nThese words are routing signals only and must never become messageText filters:\n- error\n- errors\n- exception\n- exceptions\n- failure\n- failures\n- issue\n- issues\n- creation\n- receipt creation\n- receipt processing\n- receipt\n- receipts\n- file\n- ingestion\n- import\n- upload\n- document\n- transmission\n- lockbox\n- bank\n- bank statement\n- bank stmt\n- bank file\n- remittance advice\n- remittance\n- RA advice\n- remit advice\n\nDo not use messageText LIKE for these words unless the user explicitly asks to search message text, reason, description, or error message content.\n\nExamples that must NOT create messageText filters:\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow lockbox creation errors\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"LOCKBOX\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow receipt creation errors\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow bank statement file errors\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"BANK_STATEMENT\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\n\n--------------------------------\nMESSAGE TEXT FILTER RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nUse messageText only when semanticRewrite explicitly asks to search the exception message, reason, description, seeded message text, or a specific failure reason.\n\nDo not use messageText merely because semanticRewrite contains generic routing words such as errors, exceptions, failures, creation errors, receipt creation errors, file errors, lockbox errors, bank statement errors, or remittance advice errors.\n\nUse semanticRewrite as the primary source.\nUse chatcontent only as structured fallback.\nDo not use raw user input.\n\nUse semanticRewrite as the primary source.\nUse chatcontent only as structured fallback.\nDo not use raw user input.\n\nMESSAGE TEXT TRIGGERS\n\nA messageText filter requires one of the explicit triggers below.\n\nCreate a messageText filter when semanticRewrite contains:\n\n- where <reason phrase>\n- with message <reason phrase>\n- message contains <reason phrase>\n- error contains <reason phrase>\n- exception contains <reason phrase>\n- reason contains <reason phrase>\n- description contains <reason phrase>\n- saying <reason phrase>\n- says <reason phrase>\n- because <reason phrase>\n- related to <reason phrase>\n- about <reason phrase>\n\nAlso create a messageText filter for failure phrases such as:\n\n- <thing> is missing\n- <thing> missing\n- <thing> is required\n- <thing> required\n- <thing> could not be derived\n- <thing> couldn't be derived\n- <thing> can not be derived\n- <thing> can't be derived\n- <thing> could not be retrieved\n- <thing> couldn't be retrieved\n- <thing> could not be created\n- <thing> couldn't be created\n- <thing> could not be applied\n- <thing> couldn't be applied\n- <thing> could not be selected\n- <thing> couldn't be selected\n- <thing> could not be updated\n- <thing> couldn't be updated\n- <thing> could not be processed\n- <thing> couldn't be processed\n- <thing> could not be completed\n- <thing> couldn't be completed\n- <thing> does not exist\n- <thing> doesn't exist\n- <thing> already exists\n- duplicate <thing>\n- invalid <thing>\n- <thing> is invalid\n- <thing> isn't valid\n- <thing> not found\n- <thing> is not allowed\n- <thing> isn't allowed\n- amount exceeds <thing>\n- amount is less than <thing>\n- amount is more than <thing>\n- count does not equal <thing>\n- count doesn't equal <thing>\n- currency does not match <thing>\n- currency doesn't match <thing>\n\nMESSAGE TEXT MATCHING RULE\n\nFor messageText filters, generate a grouped OR predicate.\n\nUse this structure:\n\nAND (lower(messageText) LIKE '%<direct lowercase phrase>%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%<contraction or expanded variant phrase>%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%<keyword1>%<keyword2>%<keyword3>%')\n\nRules:\n- Use LIKE, not equality, for normal user phrases.\n- Use equality only when the user provides a full exact message in quotes and explicitly asks for exact message match.\n- Always use lower(messageText).\n- Always lowercase the pattern text.\n- Escape apostrophes by doubling them.\n- Remove punctuation from keyword-reduced LIKE patterns.\n- Remove placeholder tokens such as {RCPT_NUM}, {TRX_NUM}, {CUST_NUM}, {ATTR}, {ACCOUNT_CODE}, {REMIT_ACCT}, {INPUT}, {GL_DATE}, {RECEIPT_ID}.\n- Keep meaningful business and action words in original order.\n- Do not synonym-expand.\n- Do not stem words.\n- Do not infer messageText from sourceType alone.\n- Do not infer customerName from messageText.\n- If the user says \"customer ACME\", use customerName.\n- If the user says \"customer account could not be derived\", use messageText, not customerName.\n\nCONTRACTION VARIANT RULE\n\nWhen the direct phrase contains expanded wording, add the matching contraction phrase.\n\nMappings:\n- could not -> couldn't\n- can not -> can't\n- cannot -> can't\n- was not -> wasn't\n- is not -> isn't\n- are not -> aren't\n- were not -> weren't\n- does not -> doesn't\n- do not -> don't\n- did not -> didn't\n\nWhen the direct phrase contains a contraction, add the expanded phrase.\n\nKEYWORD REDUCTION RULE\n\nAlways include one keyword-reduced LIKE pattern to avoid failures caused by contractions or grammar differences.\n\nRemove these low-value words from the keyword-reduced pattern:\n\n- is\n- are\n- was\n- were\n- be\n- been\n- being\n- can\n- cannot\n- can't\n- could\n- couldn't\n- should\n- shouldn't\n- would\n- wouldn't\n- not\n- no\n- do\n- does\n- doesn't\n- did\n- didn't\n- has\n- have\n- had\n- must\n- because\n- the\n- a\n- an\n- to\n- for\n- of\n- on\n- in\n- by\n- with\n- from\n- and\n- or\n\nKeep stable business and action words such as:\n\n- customer\n- account\n- number\n- receipt\n- lockbox\n- batch\n- bank\n- origination\n- remittance\n- advice\n- invoice\n- transaction\n- currency\n- amount\n- date\n- method\n- site\n- micr\n- accounting\n- derived\n- created\n- applied\n- retrieved\n- selected\n- processed\n- completed\n- updated\n- missing\n- invalid\n- duplicate\n- exists\n- required\n- reversed\n- accounted\n\n--------------------------------\n5. Receipt Number filter\n--------------------------------\n\nUse receiptNumber only when semanticRewrite clearly references a receipt identifier.\n\nReceipt identifier anchors:\n- receipt\n- receipt number\n- receipt id\n- receipt reference\n\nExamples:\n- receipt RTP040109-3569Z\n- receipt number RTP040109-3569Z\n- receipt id RTP040109-3569Z\n\nUse:\nAND receiptNumber = '<receipt number>'\n\nRules:\n- Preserve receiptNumber exactly as written.\n- Do not lowercase receiptNumber.\n- Do not remove dashes or special characters.\n- Do not infer receiptNumber from unrelated numeric values.\n- Do not extract receiptNumber from account numbers, transaction numbers, or customer numbers unless explicitly anchored to receipt.\n\nExamples:\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow exceptions for receipt RTP040109-3569Z\n\nOutput filter:\nAND receiptNumber = 'RTP040109-3569Z'\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow receipt creation exceptions for receipt number ABC-90001-X\n\nOutput filter:\nAND receiptNumber = 'ABC-90001-X'\n\n--------------------------------\n6. Receipt Date filter\n--------------------------------\n\nUse receiptDate when semanticRewrite explicitly refers to receipt dates.\n\nDo not map receiptDate requests to timeCreated.\n\nUse receiptDate only for receipt business dates.\n\nUse timestamp-safe bounded ranges for all receiptDate filters.\n\nNever use:\n- trunc(receiptDate)\n- BETWEEN\n- equality on receiptDate\n\nAlways use:\n- lower bound inclusive\n- upper bound exclusive\n\n--------------------------------\nRECEIPT DATE SINGLE-DAY RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nIf semanticRewrite references a specific receipt date:\n\nExamples:\n- receipt date 2026-05-20\n- receipts on 20 May 2026\n- receipts for May 20 2026\n- receipt dated 20 May\n\nUse:\n\nAND receiptDate >= TO_DATE('2026-05-20','YYYY-MM-DD')\nAND receiptDate < TO_DATE('2026-05-21','YYYY-MM-DD')\n\nIf year is missing, assume current year from sysdate.\n\n--------------------------------\nRECEIPT DATE RANGE RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nIf semanticRewrite references a receipt date range:\n\nExamples:\n- receipts between 20 May 2026 and 25 May 2026\n- receipts from 20 May to 25 May\n- receipt date between May 20 and May 25\n- receipts dated from 2026-05-20 to 2026-05-25\n\nUse inclusive lower bound and exclusive next-day upper bound.\n\nExample:\n\nAND receiptDate >= TO_DATE('2026-05-20','YYYY-MM-DD')\nAND receiptDate < TO_DATE('2026-05-26','YYYY-MM-DD')\n\nRules:\n- Add 1 day to the ending date for the upper bound.\n- Preserve timestamp-safe semantics.\n- Never use BETWEEN for receiptDate.\n\n--------------------------------\nRECEIPT DATE RELATIVE PERIOD RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nIf semanticRewrite explicitly asks for receipt dates using relative periods:\n\nExamples:\n- receipts from last 7 days\n- receipt date in last 30 days\n- receipts from past 2 weeks\n\nUse receiptDate instead of timeCreated only if the wording explicitly references receipt date.\n\nExamples:\n\nAND receiptDate > sysdate - 7\n\nAND receiptDate > sysdate - (2 * 7)\n\nIf semanticRewrite does not explicitly mention receipt date, continue using timeCreated rules.\n\n--------------------------------\nRECEIPT DATE EXAMPLES\n--------------------------------\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow receipt exceptions for receipt date 2026-05-20\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND receiptDate >= TO_DATE('2026-05-20','YYYY-MM-DD') AND receiptDate < TO_DATE('2026-05-21','YYYY-MM-DD') ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow receipt exceptions between 20 May 2026 and 25 May 2026\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND receiptDate >= TO_DATE('2026-05-20','YYYY-MM-DD') AND receiptDate < TO_DATE('2026-05-26','YYYY-MM-DD') ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow receipt exceptions for receipt RTP040109-3569Z\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND receiptNumber = 'RTP040109-3569Z' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow receipt exceptions for receipt RTP040109-3569Z on 20 May 2026\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND receiptDate >= TO_DATE('2026-05-20','YYYY-MM-DD') AND receiptDate < TO_DATE('2026-05-21','YYYY-MM-DD') AND receiptNumber = 'RTP040109-3569Z' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\n\n--------------------------------\n7. File Name / Transmission Name filter\n--------------------------------\n\nUse fileName and transmissionName only when semanticRewrite explicitly contains a file or transmission anchor followed by a value.\n\nRecognized anchors:\n- file <value>\n- file name <value>\n- filename <value>\n- fileName <value>\n- file / transmission <value>\n- file/transmission <value>\n- file or transmission <value>\n- file/transmission name <value>\n- transmission <value>\n- transmission name <value>\n- transmissionName <value>\n\nExamples:\n- file T-899399\n- file name T-899399\n- filename T-899399\n- File/Transmission 'T-899399'\n- transmission T-899399\n- transmission name T-899399\n\nCapture only the file/transmission value.\nRemove wrapping single quotes or double quotes from the captured value.\nPreserve the value casing, dashes, numbers, and special characters.\nEscape embedded apostrophes by doubling them.\n\n--------------------------------\nFILE NAME / TRANSMISSION COLUMN SELECTION\n--------------------------------\n\nIf sourceType = \"LOCKBOX\":\n- both FileName and TransmissionName anchors must generate transmissionName filter\n- LOCKBOX FileName and LOCKBOX TransmissionName mean the same filter value\n\nUse:\nAND transmissionName = '<value>'\n\nIf sourceType = \"BANK_STATEMENT\":\n- FileName, TransmissionName, and File/Transmission anchors must generate fileName filter\n\nUse:\nAND fileName = '<value>'\n\nIf sourceType = \"REMITTANCE_ADVICE\":\n- FileName, TransmissionName, and File/Transmission anchors must generate fileName filter\n\nUse:\nAND fileName = '<value>'\n\nIf sourceType = \"ALL\":\n- FileName, TransmissionName, and File/Transmission anchors must generate fileName filter\n\nUse:\nAND fileName = '<value>'\n\nDo not generate both fileName and transmissionName for the same anchored value.\nDo not generate transmissionName unless sourceType = \"LOCKBOX\".\nDo not generate fileName when sourceType = \"LOCKBOX\".\nDo not infer fileName or transmissionName from unrelated identifiers.\nDo not lowercase fileName or transmissionName values.\n\n--------------------------------\nFILE NAME / TRANSMISSION EXAMPLES\n--------------------------------\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow receipt creation errors for File/Transmission 'T-899399'\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND fileName = 'T-899399' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"yes\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow lockbox receipt creation errors for File/Transmission 'T-899399'\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND transmissionName = 'T-899399' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"LOCKBOX\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow lockbox receipt creation errors for transmission name T-899399\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND transmissionName = 'T-899399' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"LOCKBOX\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow bank statement receipt creation errors for File/Transmission 'T-899399'\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND fileName = 'T-899399' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"BANK_STATEMENT\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow bank receipt creation errors for File/Transmission 'T-899399'\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND fileName = 'T-899399' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow error detail for remittance advice File/Transmission 'T-899399'\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND fileName = 'T-899399' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"REMITTANCE_ADVICE\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"yes\"\n}\n\n\n--------------------------------\nTRANSMISSION NAME TRIGGERS\n--------------------------------\n\nGenerate transmissionName filters when semanticRewrite contains phrases like:\n\n- transmission <value>\n- transmission name <value>\n- transmissionName <value>\n- lockbox transmission <value>\n- lockbox transmission name <value>\n\nExamples:\n- transmission T-30260000000000210\n- transmission name T-30260000000000210\n- lockbox transmission T-30260000000000210\n\nUse:\nAND transmissionName = '<transmission value>'\n\n--------------------------------\nTRANSMISSION NAME RULES\n--------------------------------\n\nRules:\n- Preserve transmissionName exactly as written.\n- Do not lowercase transmissionName.\n- Do not remove dashes or special characters.\n- Do not infer transmissionName from unrelated identifiers.\n- Do not generate transmissionName filters for non-LOCKBOX requests.\n- If sourceType is not LOCKBOX, ignore transmissionName filtering entirely.\n- transmissionName filtering is allowed only for LOCKBOX sourceType.\n\n--------------------------------\nTRANSMISSION NAME EXAMPLES\n--------------------------------\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow lockbox receipt errors for transmission T-30260000000000210\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND transmissionName = 'T-30260000000000210' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"LOCKBOX\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow lockbox exceptions with transmission name T-30260000000000210\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND transmissionName = 'T-30260000000000210' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"LOCKBOX\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow all exceptions for transmission T-30260000000000210\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"yes\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow receipt exceptions for transmission T-30260000000000210\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow bank statement exceptions for transmission T-30260000000000210\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"BANK_STATEMENT\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\n8. Business Unit filter\n\nUse businessUnitName when semanticRewrite explicitly references a business unit.\n\nBusiness unit filters are valid for:\n- LOCKBOX\n- BANK_STATEMENT\n- REMITTANCE_ADVICE\n- ALL\n\n--------------------------------\nBUSINESS UNIT TRIGGERS\n--------------------------------\n\nGenerate businessUnitName filters when semanticRewrite contains phrases like:\n\n- business unit <value>\n- BU <value>\n- businessUnit <value>\n- business unit name <value>\n\nExamples:\n- business unit Vision Operations\n- BU Vision Services\n- business unit Vision Europe\n\nUse:\nAND businessUnitName = '<business unit value>'\n\n--------------------------------\nBUSINESS UNIT RULES\n--------------------------------\n\nRules:\n- Preserve businessUnitName exactly as written.\n- Do not lowercase businessUnitName.\n- Do not remove spaces or special characters.\n- Do not infer businessUnitName from unrelated organization names.\n- Do not infer businessUnitName from customerName.\n- Do not infer businessUnitName from transmissionName.\n- Business unit filtering is allowed for all source types.\n\n--------------------------------\nBUSINESS UNIT EXAMPLES\n--------------------------------\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow all receipt exceptions for business unit Vision Operations\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND businessUnitName = 'Vision Operations' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow bank statement receipt creation errors for BU Vision Services\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND businessUnitName = 'Vision Services' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"BANK_STATEMENT\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow lockbox receipt exceptions for business unit Vision Europe\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND businessUnitName = 'Vision Europe' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"LOCKBOX\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow remittance advice exceptions for BU Vision Financials\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND businessUnitName = 'Vision Financials' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"REMITTANCE_ADVICE\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"yes\"\n}\n\n--------------------------------\nCOMBINING FILTERS\n--------------------------------\n\nIf multiple filters are present, combine them in this order:\n\n1. timeCreated filters\n2. receiptDate filters\n3. amount\n4. currencyCode\n5. customerName\n6. businessUnitName\n7. receiptNumber\n8. fileName or transmissionName\n9. messageText\n10. ORDER BY clause\n11. FETCH FIRST clause\n\nEach filter condition must start with a leading space and AND.\n\nIf messageText is used, wrap all messageText alternatives in one grouped condition:\n\nAND (lower(messageText) LIKE '%...%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%...%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%...%')\n\nDo not generate multiple separate AND lower(messageText) clauses for the same message phrase.\n\n--------------------------------\nMESSAGE TEXT EXAMPLES\n--------------------------------\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow receipt errors where Customer Account Could not be derived\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND (lower(messageText) LIKE '%customer account could not be derived%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%customer account couldn''t be derived%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%customer%account%derived%') ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow lockbox errors where Lockbox number is missing\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND (lower(messageText) LIKE '%lockbox number is missing%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%lockbox%number%missing%') ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"LOCKBOX\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow lockbox exceptions where bank origination number is missing\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND (lower(messageText) LIKE '%bank origination number is missing%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%bank%origination%number%missing%') ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"LOCKBOX\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow receipt errors where receipt could not be created\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND (lower(messageText) LIKE '%receipt could not be created%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%receipt couldn''t be created%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%receipt%created%') ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nInput semanticRewrite:\nShow receipt errors for customer ACME where customer account could not be derived\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND customerName = 'ACME' AND (lower(messageText) LIKE '%customer account could not be derived%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%customer account couldn''t be derived%' OR lower(messageText) LIKE '%customer%account%derived%') ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"ALL\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\n--------------------------------\nSOURCE AND REMIT MAPPING\n--------------------------------\n\nUse semanticRewrite first.\n\nIf UserIntent is available, use it as structured confirmation.\n\nMappings:\n\nIf UserParentIntent = RECEIPT_CREATION_ERROR and UserIntent = ALL:\n- if chatcontent.remitFlag = \"Yes\" or \"yes\", return sourceType = \"ALL\", remitFlag = \"yes\"\n- if chatcontent.remitFlag = \"No\" or \"no\", return sourceType = \"ALL\", remitFlag = \"no\"\n\nIf UserIntent = LOCKBOX:\nreturn sourceType = \"LOCKBOX\", remitFlag = \"no\"\n\nIf UserIntent = BANK_STMT:\nreturn sourceType = \"BANK_STATEMENT\", remitFlag = \"no\"\n\nIf UserIntent = REMITTANCE_ADVICE:\nreturn sourceType = \"REMITTANCE_ADVICE\", remitFlag = \"yes\"\n\nLockbox Receipt Creation Exceptions:\n- semanticRewrite contains lockbox receipt creation exceptions\n- UserIntent = LOCKBOX\nReturn:\nsourceType = \"LOCKBOX\"\nremitFlag = \"no\"\n\nBank Statement Receipt Creation Exceptions:\n- semanticRewrite contains bank statement receipt creation exceptions\n- UserIntent = BANK_STMT\nReturn:\nsourceType = \"BANK_STATEMENT\"\nremitFlag = \"no\"\n\nRemittance Advice Exceptions:\n- semanticRewrite contains remittance advice exceptions\n- UserIntent = REMITTANCE_ADVICE\nReturn:\nsourceType = \"REMITTANCE_ADVICE\"\nremitFlag = \"yes\"\n\nReceipt Creation Exceptions:\n- semanticRewrite contains receipt creation exceptions\n- UserIntent = ALL and chatcontent.remitFlag = \"No\"\nReturn:\nsourceType = \"ALL\"\nremitFlag = \"no\"\n\nAll Exceptions:\n- semanticRewrite contains all exceptions, all errors, all failures, all cash processing exceptions\n- UserIntent = ALL and chatcontent.remitFlag = \"Yes\"\nReturn:\nsourceType = \"ALL\"\nremitFlag = \"yes\"\n\nFile source mappings:\n- lockbox file ingestion exceptions -> sourceType = \"LOCKBOX\", remitFlag = \"no\"\n- bank statement file exceptions -> sourceType = \"BANK_STATEMENT\", remitFlag = \"no\"\n- remittance advice file exceptions -> sourceType = \"REMITTANCE_ADVICE\", remitFlag = \"yes\"\n- broad file ingestion exceptions -> sourceType = \"ALL\", remitFlag = \"no\"\n\nIf no source is found:\n- sourceType = \"ALL\"\n- remitFlag = \"no\"\n\n--------------------------------\nBUSINESS MEANING\n--------------------------------\n\nBank Statement Exceptions:\n- sourceType = \"BANK_STATEMENT\"\n- remitFlag = \"no\"\n\nLockbox Exceptions:\n- sourceType = \"LOCKBOX\"\n- remitFlag = \"no\"\n\nRemittance Advice Exceptions:\n- sourceType = \"REMITTANCE_ADVICE\"\n- remitFlag = \"yes\"\n\nReceipt Creation Exceptions:\n- includes bank statement and lockbox receipt creation exceptions\n- does not include remittance advice exceptions\n- sourceType = \"ALL\"\n- remitFlag = \"no\"\n\nAll Exceptions:\n- includes bank statement, lockbox, and remittance advice exceptions\n- sourceType = \"ALL\"\n- remitFlag = \"yes\"\n\n--------------------------------\nFILTER RULES\n--------------------------------\n\n1. Date filter\n\nBuild date filters only on timeCreated.\n\nUse date filters when semanticRewrite mentions days, weeks, months, quarters, years, today, yesterday, this/last period, or an explicit month/quarter/year.\n\nDo not use BETWEEN.\nUse lower and upper bounds with AND.\n\nROLLING RELATIVE PERIODS\n\nUse rolling filters for phrases with a number.\n\nHours:\n- last N hours\n- past N hours\n- in last N hours\n- in the last N hours\n- last N hrs\n- past N hrs\n- last N hour\n- past N hour\n\nOutput:\nAND timeCreated > sysdate - (N / 24)\n\nDays:\n- last N days\n- last Ndays\n- past N days\n- past Ndays\n- in last N days\n- in the last N days\n\nOutput:\nAND timeCreated > sysdate - N\n\nWeeks:\n- last N weeks\n- past N weeks\n- in the last N weeks\n\nOutput:\nAND timeCreated > sysdate - (N * 7)\n\nMonths:\n- last N months\n- past N months\n- in the last N months\n\nOutput:\nAND timeCreated >= add_months(sysdate, -N)\n\nQuarters:\n- last N quarters\n- past N quarters\n- in the last N quarters\n\nOutput:\nAND timeCreated >= add_months(sysdate, -(N * 3))\n\nYears:\n- last N years\n- past N years\n- in the last N years\n\nOutput:\nAND timeCreated >= add_months(sysdate, -(N * 12))\n\n--------------------------------\nORDER BY AND FETCH RULES\n--------------------------------\n\nIn addition to filters, filterClause must also include:\n\n- ORDER BY clause\n- FETCH FIRST N ROWS ONLY clause\n\nThese clauses must appear at the end of filterClause in this order:\n\n1. filters\n2. ORDER BY\n3. FETCH FIRST\n\nExample:\nAND timeCreated > sysdate - 7 ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\n\n--------------------------------\nDEFAULT ORDERING RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nIf the user does not explicitly request sorting or ranking:\n\nUse:\nORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode\n\nAlways append:\nFETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\n\n--------------------------------\nDEFAULT FETCH RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nIf the user does not specify a row count:\n\nUse:\nFETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\n\n--------------------------------\nTOP / LIMIT DETECTION\n--------------------------------\n\nDetect phrases like:\n\n- top N\n- first N\n- highest N\n- largest N\n- biggest N\n- latest N\n- newest N\n- recent N\n- most recent N\n\nExtract N.\n\nExamples:\n- top 5\n- first 20\n- latest 10\n- most recent 15\n\nUse:\nFETCH FIRST N ROWS ONLY\n\n--------------------------------\nSORT DETECTION RULES\n--------------------------------\n\nUse semanticRewrite as the primary source.\n\nIf no explicit sorting intent exists:\nORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode\n\n--------------------------------\nMOST RECENT / LATEST SORTING\n--------------------------------\n\nIf semanticRewrite contains phrases like:\n\n- most recent\n- latest\n- newest\n- recent\n- recently created\n\nUse:\nORDER BY timeCreated DESC, amount DESC\n\n--------------------------------\nHIGHEST / TOP / LARGEST AMOUNT SORTING\n--------------------------------\n\nIf semanticRewrite contains phrases like:\n\n- top\n- highest\n- largest\n- biggest\n- maximum amount\n- highest amount\n\nAnd no explicit recent/latest wording exists:\n\nUse:\nORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode\n\n--------------------------------\nLOWEST / SMALLEST AMOUNT SORTING\n--------------------------------\n\nIf semanticRewrite contains phrases like:\n\n- lowest\n- smallest\n- minimum amount\n- least amount\n\nUse:\nORDER BY amount ASC, currencyCode\n\n--------------------------------\nOLDEST SORTING\n--------------------------------\n\nIf semanticRewrite contains phrases like:\n\n- oldest\n- earliest\n\nUse:\nORDER BY timeCreated ASC, amount DESC\n\n--------------------------------\nSECONDARY SORT RULE\n--------------------------------\n\nWhen sorting by timeCreated:\n\nUse amount DESC as the secondary sort field.\n\n--------------------------------\nVALID ORDER BY COLUMNS\n--------------------------------\n\nUse only these columns inside ORDER BY:\n\n- timeCreated\n- amount\n- currencyCode\n- customerName\n- receiptDate\n- receiptNumber\n- transmissionName\n- fileName\n\nDo not use any other columns.\n\n--------------------------------\nCASE PRIORITY RULES\n--------------------------------\n\nIf semanticRewrite contains both:\n- top/highest\nAND\n- most recent/latest/newest\n\nThen prioritize recency sorting.\n\nExample:\ntop 5 most recent receipts\n\nUse:\nORDER BY timeCreated DESC, amount DESC\nFETCH FIRST 5 ROWS ONLY\n\n--------------------------------\nCOMBINING FILTERS\n--------------------------------\n\nIf multiple filters are present, combine them in this order:\n\n1. timeCreated filters\n2. receiptDate filters\n3. amount\n4. currencyCode\n5. customerName\n6. businessUnitName\n7. receiptNumber\n8. transmissionName\n9. messageText\n10. ORDER BY clause\n11. FETCH FIRST clause\n\nExamples:\n{\n  \"filterClause\": \" AND timeCreated > sysdate - 7 AND amount >= 50000 AND currencyCode = 'USD' ORDER BY amount DESC, currencyCode FETCH FIRST 500 ROWS ONLY\",\n  \"sourceType\": \"LOCKBOX\",\n  \"remitFlag\": \"no\"\n}\n\nKeep exactly one space between tokens.\nThe filterClause string may begin with a leading space.\n\n--------------------------------\nFETCH CLAUSE RULES\n--------------------------------\n\nAlways generate FETCH FIRST clause.\n\nSyntax:\nFETCH FIRST N ROWS ONLY\n\nNever use:\n- LIMIT\n- TOP\n- ROWNUM\n\n--------------------------------\nENTITY FALLBACK\n--------------------------------\n\nIf semanticRewrite does not contain a filter but chatcontent.entitiesExtracted contains one, use the entity fallback.\n\nExamples:\n\nIf chatcontent.entitiesExtracted.dateRange = \"last 12 days\":\nfilterClause includes:\nAND timeCreated > sysdate - 12\n\nIf chatcontent.entitiesExtracted.currencyCode = \"USD\":\nfilterClause includes:\nAND currencyCode = 'USD'\n\nIf chatcontent.entitiesExtracted.customerName = \"Randy Brown\":\nfilterClause includes:\nAND customerName = 'Randy Brown'\n\nIf semanticRewrite already contains a different explicit filter, semanticRewrite wins.\n\n--------------------------------\nDO NOT DO THESE\n--------------------------------\n\n- Do not read raw userInput for filter extraction\n- Do not use {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Do not invent filters not present in semanticRewrite or chatcontent.entitiesExtracted\n- Do not default days\n- Do not default currency\n- Do not default amount\n- Do not include sourceType inside filterClause\n- Do not include remitFlag inside filterClause\n- Do not return null for filterClause\n- Do not return null for sourceType\n- Do not return null for remitFlag\n- Do not use BETWEEN\n- Do not extract customerName from unanchored literals\n- Do not omit ORDER BY\n- Do not omit FETCH FIRST\n- Do not use invalid columns in ORDER BY\n- Do not use LIMIT\n- Do not use TOP keyword in SQL\n- Do not generate multiple ORDER BY clauses\n- Do not generate multiple FETCH clauses\n- Do not place FETCH before ORDER BY\n- Do not use lowercase sql keywords inside ORDER BY/FETCH fragments\n- Do not use equality on receiptDate\n- Do not use BETWEEN for receiptDate\n- Do not map receiptDate filters to timeCreated\n- Do not infer receiptNumber from account numbers or transaction numbers\n- Do not lowercase receiptNumber\n- Do not infer transmissionName from unrelated identifiers\n- Do not lowercase transmissionName\n- Do not generate transmissionName filters unless sourceType is LOCKBOX\n- Do not generate fileName filters when sourceType is LOCKBOX\n- For LOCKBOX, FileName and TransmissionName anchors must both use transmissionName\n- For ALL, BANK_STATEMENT, and REMITTANCE_ADVICE, FileName and TransmissionName anchors must use fileName\n- Do not generate both fileName and transmissionName for the same anchored value\n- Do not infer businessUnitName from customer names\n- Do not infer businessUnitName from organization names unless explicitly anchored\n- Do not lowercase businessUnitName\n- Do not remove spaces from businessUnitName\n- Do not output anything except the JSON object\n- Do not generate messageText filters from intent words such as creation errors, receipt creation errors, file errors, lockbox errors, bank statement errors, remittance advice errors, exceptions, failures, or issues.\n- Do not create lower(messageText) LIKE filters unless the user explicitly asks for message, reason, description, says, saying, because, related to, about, missing, invalid, duplicate, required, could not be derived, could not be created, or another specific failure reason.\n\n\n\n--------------------------------\nFINAL INSTRUCTION\n--------------------------------\n\nRead only semanticRewrite:\n{{$context.$variables.semanticrewrite}}\n\nUse chatcontent only as structured fallback.\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object with:\n- filterClause\n- sourceType\n- remitFlag"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"sourceType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"LOCKBOX\",\n        \"BANK_STATEMENT\",\n        \"REMITTANCE_ADVICE\",\n        \"ALL\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"filterClause\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"remitFlag\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"yes\",\n        \"no\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"sourceType\",\n    \"filterClause\",\n    \"remitFlag\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "datarollup",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "// --- Input ---\n\nvar inputData = null;\nvar tempdata = $context.$nodes.RECEIPTINQUIRY.$output.output;\n// inputData = $context.$nodes.RECEIPTINQUIRY.$output;\n\nconst outer = JSON.parse(tempdata);\nconst output = JSON.parse(tempdata);\n\nconst receipts = output.result.receipts;\nconst application = output.result.application;\nconst reference = output.result.reference;\n\ninputData = receipts;\n\nvar debug = {};\n\n// --- Configuration ---\n\n// Over threshold, roll up only AMOUNTREMAINING.\nvar ROLLUP_MEASURES = [\n  \"amountRemaining\"\n];\n\n// Below this threshold: return raw records, except CASHRECEIPTID is still dropped.\nvar ROLLUP_THRESHOLD = 10;\n\n// Fields that must always appear in output rows regardless of uniformity.\nvar PRESERVE_FIELDS = [\n  \"currency\",\n  \"currencycode\",\n  \"currencytype\",\n  \"currencysymbol\",\n  \"receiptCurrencyCode\"\n];\n\n// Fields to remove before any processing.\n// This runs before empty/single-record/threshold logic.\nvar DROP_FIELDS = [\n  \"cashreceiptid\"\n];\n\n// Required over-threshold grouping:\n// BUSINESSUNITNAME + CUSTOMERNAME + CUSTOMERACCOUNTNUMBER + RECEIPTCURRENCYCODE.\n// BUSINESSUNITNAME is included only when it varies across records.\nvar REQUIRED_GROUP_FIELDS = [\n  \"businessunitname\",\n  \"customername\",\n  \"customeraccountnumber\",\n  \"receiptcurrencycode\"\n];\n\nvar BUSINESS_UNIT_FIELD_CANDIDATES = [\n  \"businessUnitName\",\n  \"BUSINESSUNITNAME\",\n  \"businessunitname\",\n  \"businessUnit\",\n  \"BUSINESSUNIT\",\n  \"businessunit\",\n  \"buName\",\n  \"BUNAME\",\n  \"buname\"\n];\n\n// --- Parse input ---\n\nvar raw;\ntry {\n  raw = typeof inputData === \"string\" ? JSON.parse(inputData) : inputData;\n} catch (e) {\n  raw = null;\n}\n\nvar records = Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : ((raw && raw.data) ? raw.data : []);\n\n// --- Generic helpers ---\n\nfunction getValueIgnoreCase(obj, possibleKeys) {\n  if (!obj || typeof obj !== \"object\") return null;\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < possibleKeys.length; i++) {\n    var wanted = String(possibleKeys[i]).toLowerCase();\n\n    for (var k in obj) {\n      if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(obj, k)) continue;\n\n      if (String(k).toLowerCase() === wanted) {\n        return obj[k];\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction getSemanticRewriteText() {\n  return $context &&\n    $context.$variables &&\n    $context.$variables.chatcontext &&\n    $context.$variables.chatcontext.semantic_rewrite\n      ? String($context.$variables.chatcontext.semantic_rewrite)\n      : \"\";\n}\n\nfunction normalizeDisplayText(text) {\n  if (text == null) return \"\";\n\n  var value = String(text).trim();\n\n  if (!value) return \"\";\n\n  if (value.charAt(value.length - 1) !== \".\") {\n    value += \".\";\n  }\n\n  return value;\n}\n\nfunction getChatContextEntity(name) {\n  return $context &&\n    $context.$variables &&\n    $context.$variables.chatcontext &&\n    $context.$variables.chatcontext.entities_extracted\n      ? $context.$variables.chatcontext.entities_extracted[name]\n      : null;\n}\n\nfunction getAmountRemainingValue(row) {\n  return getValueIgnoreCase(row, [\n    \"amountRemaining\",\n    \"AMOUNTREMAINING\",\n    \"amountremaining\"\n  ]);\n}\n\nfunction getCurrencyValue(row) {\n  return getValueIgnoreCase(row, [\n    \"receiptCurrencyCode\",\n    \"RECEIPTCURRENCYCODE\",\n    \"receiptcurrencycode\",\n    \"currencyCode\",\n    \"CURRENCYCODE\",\n    \"currencycode\",\n    \"currency\",\n    \"CURRENCY\"\n  ]);\n}\n\nfunction getCustomerValue(row) {\n  return getValueIgnoreCase(row, [\n    \"customerName\",\n    \"CUSTOMERNAME\",\n    \"customername\",\n    \"customer\"\n  ]);\n}\n\nfunction getAccountValue(row) {\n  return getValueIgnoreCase(row, [\n    \"customerAccountNumber\",\n    \"CUSTOMERACCOUNTNUMBER\",\n    \"customeraccountnumber\",\n    \"accountNumber\",\n    \"ACCOUNTNUMBER\",\n    \"accountnumber\"\n  ]);\n}\n\nfunction getReceiptNumberValue(row) {\n  return getValueIgnoreCase(row, [\n    \"receiptNumber\",\n    \"RECEIPTNUMBER\",\n    \"receiptnumber\"\n  ]);\n}\n\nfunction getReceiptDateValue(row) {\n  return getValueIgnoreCase(row, [\n    \"receiptDate\",\n    \"RECEIPTDATE\",\n    \"receiptdate\",\n    \"accountingDate\",\n    \"ACCOUNTINGDATE\",\n    \"accountingdate\",\n    \"creationDate\",\n    \"CREATIONDATE\",\n    \"creationdate\",\n    \"timeCreated\",\n    \"TIMECREATED\",\n    \"timecreated\"\n  ]);\n}\n\nfunction getBusinessUnitValue(row) {\n  return getValueIgnoreCase(row, BUSINESS_UNIT_FIELD_CANDIDATES);\n}\n\nfunction parseDateValue(value) {\n  if (value == null || value === \"\") return null;\n\n  var d = new Date(value);\n\n  if (isNaN(d.getTime())) return null;\n\n  return d;\n}\n\nfunction ageInDaysFromToday(dateValue) {\n  var d = parseDateValue(dateValue);\n\n  if (!d) return null;\n\n  var today = new Date();\n\n  var todayUtc = Date.UTC(\n    today.getFullYear(),\n    today.getMonth(),\n    today.getDate()\n  );\n\n  var dateUtc = Date.UTC(\n    d.getFullYear(),\n    d.getMonth(),\n    d.getDate()\n  );\n\n  var diffMs = todayUtc - dateUtc;\n\n  return Math.floor(diffMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n}\n\nfunction formatAmount(amount) {\n  if (amount == null || isNaN(Number(amount))) return \"unknown amount\";\n\n  return Number(amount).toLocaleString(undefined, {\n    minimumFractionDigits: 2,\n    maximumFractionDigits: 2\n  });\n}\n\nfunction formatAmountWithCurrency(amount, currency) {\n  var formattedAmount = formatAmount(amount);\n\n  if (currency == null || currency === \"\") {\n    return formattedAmount;\n  }\n\n  return formattedAmount + \" \" + currency;\n}\n\nfunction countDistinct(rows, getterFn) {\n  var seen = {};\n  var count = 0;\n\n  if (!rows) return 0;\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {\n    var value = getterFn(rows[i]);\n\n    if (value == null || value === \"\") continue;\n\n    var key = String(value);\n\n    if (!seen[key]) {\n      seen[key] = true;\n      count++;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return count;\n}\n\nfunction sumAmountRemaining(rows) {\n  var total = 0;\n\n  if (!rows) return 0;\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {\n    var value = getAmountRemainingValue(rows[i]);\n    var num = Number(value);\n\n    if (value != null && !isNaN(num)) {\n      total += num;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return Math.round(total * 100) / 100;\n}\n\nfunction getUniformBusinessUnitInfo(rows) {\n  var info = {\n    hasBusinessUnitField: false,\n    isUniform: false,\n    value: null,\n    fieldName: null\n  };\n\n  if (!rows || !rows.length) {\n    return info;\n  }\n\n  var firstRow = rows[0];\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < BUSINESS_UNIT_FIELD_CANDIDATES.length; i++) {\n    var candidate = String(BUSINESS_UNIT_FIELD_CANDIDATES[i]).toLowerCase();\n\n    for (var k in firstRow) {\n      if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(firstRow, k)) continue;\n\n      if (String(k).toLowerCase() === candidate) {\n        info.hasBusinessUnitField = true;\n        info.fieldName = k;\n        info.value = firstRow[k];\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (info.hasBusinessUnitField) break;\n  }\n\n  if (!info.hasBusinessUnitField) {\n    return info;\n  }\n\n  var firstNorm = info.value == null ? \"\" : String(info.value);\n  var uniform = true;\n\n  for (var r = 1; r < rows.length; r++) {\n    var currentValue = getBusinessUnitValue(rows[r]);\n    var currentNorm = currentValue == null ? \"\" : String(currentValue);\n\n    if (currentNorm !== firstNorm) {\n      uniform = false;\n      break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  info.isUniform = uniform;\n\n  return info;\n}\n\nfunction removeFieldIgnoreCaseFromRows(rows, fieldName) {\n  if (!rows || !rows.length || !fieldName) {\n    return rows || [];\n  }\n\n  var fieldLower = String(fieldName).toLowerCase();\n  var outputRows = [];\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {\n    var src = rows[i];\n    var cleaned = {};\n\n    if (src && typeof src === \"object\") {\n      for (var k in src) {\n        if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(src, k)) continue;\n\n        if (String(k).toLowerCase() === fieldLower) continue;\n\n        cleaned[k] = src[k];\n      }\n    }\n\n    outputRows.push(cleaned);\n  }\n\n  return outputRows;\n}\n\nfunction buildBusinessUnitPhraseFromRows(rows, uniformBusinessUnitName) {\n  if (uniformBusinessUnitName) {\n    return \" for \" + uniformBusinessUnitName;\n  }\n\n  var businessUnitCount = countDistinct(rows, getBusinessUnitValue);\n\n  if (businessUnitCount > 1) {\n    return \" across \" + businessUnitCount + \" business units\";\n  }\n\n  var buFromRows = rows && rows.length ? getBusinessUnitValue(rows[0]) : null;\n\n  if (buFromRows) {\n    return \" for \" + buFromRows;\n  }\n\n  return \"\";\n}\n\nfunction getTopCustomersByAmount(rows, maxCount) {\n  var totalsByCustomer = {};\n  var orderedCustomers = [];\n\n  if (!rows || !rows.length) return [];\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {\n    var row = rows[i];\n    var customerName = getCustomerValue(row);\n\n    if (!customerName) continue;\n\n    var amountValue = getAmountRemainingValue(row);\n    var amountNumber = Number(amountValue);\n\n    if (amountValue == null || isNaN(amountNumber)) {\n      amountNumber = 0;\n    }\n\n    var key = String(customerName);\n\n    if (!totalsByCustomer[key]) {\n      totalsByCustomer[key] = {\n        customerName: customerName,\n        amount: 0\n      };\n      orderedCustomers.push(key);\n    }\n\n    totalsByCustomer[key].amount += Math.abs(amountNumber);\n  }\n\n  orderedCustomers.sort(function(a, b) {\n    return totalsByCustomer[b].amount - totalsByCustomer[a].amount;\n  });\n\n  var result = [];\n\n  for (var j = 0; j < orderedCustomers.length && result.length < maxCount; j++) {\n    result.push(totalsByCustomer[orderedCustomers[j]].customerName);\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n\nfunction extractHighlightedCustomersFromSummary(summaryText) {\n  var customers = [];\n\n  if (!summaryText) return customers;\n\n  var text = String(summaryText);\n\n  var patterns = [\n    /Customer with the highest unapplied amount is ([^,.]+)/i,\n    /for Customer ([^,.]+)/i,\n    /for customer ([^,.]+)/i\n  ];\n\n  for (var p = 0; p < patterns.length; p++) {\n    var match = text.match(patterns[p]);\n\n    if (match && match[1]) {\n      customers.push(match[1].trim());\n    }\n  }\n\n  return customers;\n}\n\nfunction uniqueStrings(values) {\n  var seen = {};\n  var result = [];\n\n  if (!values) return result;\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {\n    var value = values[i];\n\n    if (value == null || value === \"\") continue;\n\n    var key = String(value).toLowerCase();\n\n    if (!seen[key]) {\n      seen[key] = true;\n      result.push(String(value));\n    }\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n\nfunction buildSuggestionsText(rows, summaryText) {\n  var suggestions = [];\n\n  var firstRow = rows && rows.length ? rows[0] : null;\n  var receiptNumber = firstRow ? getReceiptNumberValue(firstRow) : null;\n\n  // For receipt-level results, use receipt-specific suggestions.\n  if (receiptNumber && rows && rows.length === 1) {\n    suggestions.push(\"Show invoice matches for receipt \" + receiptNumber);\n    suggestions.push(\"Show promise matches for receipt \" + receiptNumber);\n    suggestions.push(\"Show receipt source for receipt \" + receiptNumber);\n\n    return suggestions.map(function(s) {\n      return \"• \" + s;\n    }).join(\"\\n\");\n  }\n\n  // Prefer customers explicitly highlighted in the summary.\n  var customers = extractHighlightedCustomersFromSummary(summaryText);\n\n  // If summary did not expose a customer cleanly, use top customer(s) from rows by amount.\n  if (!customers.length) {\n    customers = getTopCustomersByAmount(rows, 2);\n  }\n\n  customers = uniqueStrings(customers).slice(0, 2);\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < customers.length; i++) {\n    var customerName = customers[i];\n\n    suggestions.push(\"Show unapplied receipts for \" + customerName);\n    suggestions.push(\"Show open invoices for \" + customerName);\n  }\n\n  // Keep the list compact and avoid generic hardcoded customer names.\n  suggestions = uniqueStrings(suggestions).slice(0, 4);\n\n  return suggestions.map(function(s) {\n    return \"• \" + s;\n  }).join(\"\\n\");\n}\n\n// --- Summary helpers ---\n\nfunction buildNoRollupSummaryText(rows, uniformBusinessUnitName) {\n  var recordCount = rows && rows.length ? rows.length : 0;\n\n  if (!rows || !rows.length) {\n    var noDataText = \"No unapplied receipt records were found\";\n\n    if (uniformBusinessUnitName) {\n      noDataText += \" for \" + uniformBusinessUnitName;\n    }\n\n    return noDataText + \".\";\n  }\n\n  var totalAmount = sumAmountRemaining(rows);\n  var currency = getCurrencyValue(rows[0]);\n  var businessUnitPhrase = buildBusinessUnitPhraseFromRows(rows, uniformBusinessUnitName);\n\n  var oldestAge = null;\n  var oldestDateValue = null;\n  var oldestRow = null;\n\n  var highestAmount = null;\n  var highestAmountRow = null;\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {\n    var row = rows[i];\n\n    var receiptDate = getReceiptDateValue(row);\n    var ageDays = ageInDaysFromToday(receiptDate);\n\n    if (ageDays != null && (oldestAge == null || ageDays > oldestAge)) {\n      oldestAge = ageDays;\n      oldestDateValue = receiptDate;\n      oldestRow = row;\n    }\n\n    var amountValue = getAmountRemainingValue(row);\n    var amountNumber = Number(amountValue);\n\n    if (amountValue != null && !isNaN(amountNumber)) {\n      var comparableAmount = Math.abs(amountNumber);\n\n      if (highestAmount == null || comparableAmount > highestAmount) {\n        highestAmount = comparableAmount;\n        highestAmountRow = row;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  var text =\n    \"Found \" +\n    recordCount +\n    \" unapplied receipt record\" +\n    (recordCount === 1 ? \"\" : \"s\") +\n    \", totalling \" +\n    formatAmountWithCurrency(totalAmount, currency) +\n    businessUnitPhrase +\n    \".\";\n\n  if (oldestAge != null) {\n    var oldestReceiptNumber = getReceiptNumberValue(oldestRow);\n\n    text +=\n      \" The oldest unapplied receipt is \" +\n      (oldestReceiptNumber ? oldestReceiptNumber + \" \" : \"\") +\n      oldestAge +\n      \" days old\";\n\n    if (oldestDateValue != null && oldestDateValue !== \"\") {\n      text += \" with receipt date \" + oldestDateValue;\n    }\n\n    text += \".\";\n  }\n\n  if (highestAmountRow) {\n    var receiptNumber = getReceiptNumberValue(highestAmountRow);\n    var customerName = getCustomerValue(highestAmountRow);\n    var accountNumber = getAccountValue(highestAmountRow);\n    var highestCurrency = getCurrencyValue(highestAmountRow);\n\n    text +=\n      \" The highest amount receipt is \" +\n      (receiptNumber ? receiptNumber + \" \" : \"\") +\n      \"for \" +\n      formatAmountWithCurrency(highestAmount, highestCurrency);\n\n    if (customerName) {\n      text += \" for Customer \" + customerName;\n    }\n\n    if (accountNumber) {\n      text += \", Account# \" + accountNumber;\n    }\n\n    text += \".\";\n  }\n\n  return text;\n}\n\nfunction buildRollupSummaryText(rows, originalRecordCount, uniformBusinessUnitName) {\n  var recordCount = originalRecordCount || 0;\n\n  if (!rows || !rows.length) {\n    var noDataText = \"Found \" + recordCount + \" unapplied receipt records\";\n\n    if (uniformBusinessUnitName) {\n      noDataText += \" for \" + uniformBusinessUnitName;\n    }\n\n    return noDataText + \".\";\n  }\n\n  var totalAmount = sumAmountRemaining(rows);\n  var customerCount = countDistinct(rows, getCustomerValue);\n  var currency = getCurrencyValue(rows[0]);\n  var businessUnitPhrase = buildBusinessUnitPhraseFromRows(rows, uniformBusinessUnitName);\n\n  var highestAmount = null;\n  var highestRow = null;\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {\n    var row = rows[i];\n\n    var amountValue = getAmountRemainingValue(row);\n    var amountNumber = Number(amountValue);\n\n    if (amountValue != null && !isNaN(amountNumber)) {\n      var comparableAmount = Math.abs(amountNumber);\n\n      if (highestAmount == null || comparableAmount > highestAmount) {\n        highestAmount = comparableAmount;\n        highestRow = row;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  var text =\n    recordCount +\n    \" unapplied receipt record\" +\n    (recordCount === 1 ? \"\" : \"s\") +\n    \" across \" +\n    customerCount +\n    \" Customer\" +\n    (customerCount === 1 ? \"\" : \"s\") +\n    \", totalling \" +\n    formatAmountWithCurrency(totalAmount, currency) +\n    businessUnitPhrase +\n    \", sorted by amount remaining highest to lowest.\";\n\n  if (highestRow) {\n    var customerName = getCustomerValue(highestRow);\n    var accountNumber = getAccountValue(highestRow);\n    var highestCurrency = getCurrencyValue(highestRow);\n    var businessUnitName = getBusinessUnitValue(highestRow);\n\n    text +=\n      \" The Customer with the highest unapplied amount is \" +\n      (customerName || \"unknown Customer\");\n\n    if (accountNumber) {\n      text += \", Account# \" + accountNumber;\n    }\n\n    if (!uniformBusinessUnitName && businessUnitName) {\n      text += \", Business Unit \" + businessUnitName;\n    }\n\n    text +=\n      \", with \" +\n      formatAmountWithCurrency(highestAmount, highestCurrency) +\n      \".\";\n  }\n\n  return text;\n}\n\n// --- Drop fields as first data-normalization step ----\n// Must run before empty/single-record/threshold bypasses.\n// Preserves original field order for all remaining columns.\n\nif (records && records.length > 0) {\n  var dropFieldSet = {};\n  for (var df = 0; df < DROP_FIELDS.length; df++) {\n    dropFieldSet[String(DROP_FIELDS[df]).toLowerCase()] = true;\n  }\n\n  var cleanedRecords = [];\n\n  for (var r = 0; r < records.length; r++) {\n    var src = records[r];\n    var cleaned = {};\n\n    if (src && typeof src === \"object\") {\n      for (var field in src) {\n        if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(src, field)) continue;\n\n        if (dropFieldSet[String(field).toLowerCase()]) continue;\n\n        cleaned[field] = src[field];\n      }\n    }\n\n    cleanedRecords.push(cleaned);\n  }\n\n  records = cleanedRecords;\n}\n\n// --- Uniform Business Unit handling ---\n// If businessUnitName is same for all records, remove it from output rows\n// and keep its value for summary text.\n// If it varies, keep it so it becomes part of rollup grouping.\n\nvar businessUnitInfo = getUniformBusinessUnitInfo(records);\nvar uniformBusinessUnitName =\n  businessUnitInfo && businessUnitInfo.isUniform\n    ? businessUnitInfo.value\n    : null;\n\nif (businessUnitInfo && businessUnitInfo.isUniform && businessUnitInfo.fieldName) {\n  records = removeFieldIgnoreCaseFromRows(records, businessUnitInfo.fieldName);\n}\n\nvar aggregatedData = [];\nvar repeatAttributes = [];\nvar groupByKeys = [];\nvar rollupFields = [];\nvar chosenLevel = null;\n\n// --- Common output helpers ---\n\nfunction buildOutput(dataRows, aggregateRows, repeats, summaryText, dbg) {\n  return {\n    data: dataRows,\n    application: application,\n    remitref: reference,\n    aggregatedData: aggregateRows,\n    repeatAttributes: repeats,\n    summary: summaryText,\n    filterText: normalizeDisplayText(getSemanticRewriteText()),\n    suggestions: buildSuggestionsText(dataRows),\n    debug: dbg\n  };\n}\n\n// --- Early return: empty ---\n\nif (!records || !records.length) {\n  debug.rollup = {\n    recordCount: 0,\n    groupCount: 0,\n    groupByKeys: [],\n    rollupFields: [],\n    repeatAttributes: [],\n    chosenLevel: null\n  };\n\n  return buildOutput(\n    [],\n    [],\n    [],\n    buildNoRollupSummaryText([], uniformBusinessUnitName),\n    debug\n  );\n}\n\n// --- Single-record pass-through ---\n// Exactly one record: nothing to summarize, group, or lift.\n// CASHRECEIPTID has already been removed.\n\nif (records.length === 1) {\n  debug.rollup = {\n    recordCount: 1,\n    groupCount: 1,\n    groupByKeys: [],\n    rollupFields: [],\n    repeatAttributes: [],\n    chosenLevel: null,\n    bypassed: true,\n    reason: \"recordCount === 1, pass-through after field cleanup\"\n  };\n\n  return buildOutput(\n    records,\n    records,\n    [],\n    buildNoRollupSummaryText(records, uniformBusinessUnitName),\n    debug\n  );\n}\n\n// --- Below-threshold bypass ----\n// 2–10 records: no uniform-attribute stripping, no grouping.\n// Return records after required field cleanup.\n\nif (records.length <= ROLLUP_THRESHOLD) {\n  debug.rollup = {\n    recordCount: records.length,\n    groupCount: records.length,\n    groupByKeys: [],\n    rollupFields: [],\n    repeatAttributes: [],\n    chosenLevel: null,\n    bypassed: true,\n    threshold: ROLLUP_THRESHOLD,\n    reason: \"recordCount <= threshold, raw pass-through after field cleanup\"\n  };\n\n  return buildOutput(\n    records,\n    records,\n    [],\n    buildNoRollupSummaryText(records, uniformBusinessUnitName),\n    debug\n  );\n}\n\n// ---\n// Everything below only executes when records.length > ROLLUP_THRESHOLD\n// ---\n\n\nvar i, j, k;\nvar lowerKey;\nvar rec;\nvar actualKey;\nvar attrKey;\nvar attrKeyLower;\nvar firstVal, firstNorm;\nvar currentVal, currentNorm;\nvar isUniform;\nvar groupKey;\nvar groupVal;\nvar value;\nvar num;\nvar row;\nvar tempRow;\n\n// --- Key map and normalization ---\n\nvar keyMap = {};\nvar allKeys = [];\nvar allKeySet = {};\nvar normalizedRecords = [];\n\nfor (i = 0; i < records.length; i++) {\n  rec = records[i];\n  normalizedRecords[i] = {};\n\n  if (!rec || typeof rec !== \"object\") continue;\n\n  for (k in rec) {\n    if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(rec, k)) {\n      lowerKey = String(k).toLowerCase();\n\n      normalizedRecords[i][lowerKey] = rec[k];\n\n      if (!keyMap[lowerKey]) {\n        keyMap[lowerKey] = k;\n      }\n\n      if (!allKeySet[lowerKey]) {\n        allKeySet[lowerKey] = true;\n        allKeys.push(k);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// --- Helpers ---\n\nfunction resolveKey(lowerName) {\n  return keyMap[String(lowerName).toLowerCase()] || null;\n}\n\nfunction pushIfPresent(arr, key) {\n  if (!key) return;\n\n  var keyLower = String(key).toLowerCase();\n\n  for (var x = 0; x < arr.length; x++) {\n    if (String(arr[x]).toLowerCase() === keyLower) return;\n  }\n\n  arr.push(key);\n}\n\nfunction containsKeyIgnoreCase(arr, key) {\n  if (!key) return false;\n\n  var keyLower = String(key).toLowerCase();\n\n  for (var x = 0; x < arr.length; x++) {\n    if (String(arr[x]).toLowerCase() === keyLower) return true;\n  }\n\n  return false;\n}\n\n// --- Identify required group keys ---\n// Required grouping over threshold:\n// BUSINESSUNITNAME when varying + CUSTOMERNAME + ACCOUNTNUMBER + RECEIPTCURRENCYCODE.\n// If one of these fields is absent, use the fields that are present,\n// but still require AMOUNTREMAINING to aggregate.\n\nvar businessUnitKey =\n  resolveKey(\"businessunitname\") ||\n  resolveKey(\"businessunit\") ||\n  resolveKey(\"buname\");\n\nvar custKey = resolveKey(\"customername\");\nvar accKey = resolveKey(\"customeraccountnumber\");\nvar receiptCurrKey = resolveKey(\"receiptcurrencycode\");\n\n// --- Bypass rollup if all records belong to same customer + account --------\n// If CUSTOMERNAME and CUSTOMERACCOUNTNUMBER are same across all records,\n// return raw cleaned records instead of grouping.\n// Exception: if Business Unit varies, continue rollup by BU + customer/account/currency.\n\nfunction allRecordsSameCustomerAndAccount() {\n  if (!custKey || !accKey) return false;\n\n  var custLower = String(custKey).toLowerCase();\n  var accLower = String(accKey).toLowerCase();\n\n  var firstCustomer = normalizedRecords[0][custLower];\n  var firstAccount = normalizedRecords[0][accLower];\n\n  var firstCustomerNorm = firstCustomer == null ? \"\" : String(firstCustomer);\n  var firstAccountNorm = firstAccount == null ? \"\" : String(firstAccount);\n\n  for (var s = 1; s < normalizedRecords.length; s++) {\n    var currentCustomer = normalizedRecords[s][custLower];\n    var currentAccount = normalizedRecords[s][accLower];\n\n    var currentCustomerNorm = currentCustomer == null ? \"\" : String(currentCustomer);\n    var currentAccountNorm = currentAccount == null ? \"\" : String(currentAccount);\n\n    if (\n      currentCustomerNorm !== firstCustomerNorm ||\n      currentAccountNorm !== firstAccountNorm\n    ) {\n      return false;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return true;\n}\n\nif (allRecordsSameCustomerAndAccount() && !businessUnitKey) {\n  debug.rollup = {\n    recordCount: records.length,\n    groupCount: records.length,\n    groupByKeys: [],\n    rollupFields: [],\n    repeatAttributes: [],\n    chosenLevel: null,\n    bypassed: true,\n    reason: \"All records have the same CUSTOMERNAME and CUSTOMERACCOUNTNUMBER and Business Unit is not varying; rollup skipped.\"\n  };\n\n  return buildOutput(\n    records,\n    records,\n    [],\n    buildNoRollupSummaryText(records, uniformBusinessUnitName),\n    debug\n  );\n}\n\n// Business Unit is only present here if it varied across rows.\n// Uniform Business Unit was removed before this point.\npushIfPresent(groupByKeys, businessUnitKey);\npushIfPresent(groupByKeys, custKey);\npushIfPresent(groupByKeys, accKey);\npushIfPresent(groupByKeys, receiptCurrKey);\n\nvar forcedGroupKeySet = {};\n\nfor (i = 0; i < groupByKeys.length; i++) {\n  forcedGroupKeySet[String(groupByKeys[i]).toLowerCase()] = true;\n}\n\n// --- Identify rollup measures actually present ---\n// Sum only AMOUNTREMAINING.\n\nvar presentRollups = [];\nvar rollupKeySet = {};\n\nactualKey = resolveKey(\"amountremaining\");\n\nif (actualKey) {\n  presentRollups.push(actualKey);\n  rollupFields.push(actualKey);\n  rollupKeySet[String(actualKey).toLowerCase()] = true;\n}\n\nvar canGroup = groupByKeys.length > 0 && presentRollups.length > 0;\n\n// --- Pass 1: detect uniform attributes ----\n// Runs only when records.length > ROLLUP_THRESHOLD.\n// Uniform columns are lifted to repeatAttributes and stripped from rows.\n// Required group-by fields and rollup measures are never lifted.\n\nvar preserveKeySet = {};\n\nfor (i = 0; i < PRESERVE_FIELDS.length; i++) {\n  preserveKeySet[String(PRESERVE_FIELDS[i]).toLowerCase()] = true;\n}\n\nvar uniformKeySet = {};\nvar preservedVaryingKeySet = {};\n\nfor (i = 0; i < allKeys.length; i++) {\n  attrKey = allKeys[i];\n  attrKeyLower = String(attrKey).toLowerCase();\n\n  // Rollup measures are never lifted as repeat attributes.\n  if (rollupKeySet[attrKeyLower]) continue;\n\n  // Required group-by fields are never lifted as repeat attributes.\n  if (forcedGroupKeySet[attrKeyLower]) continue;\n\n  firstVal = normalizedRecords[0][attrKeyLower];\n  firstNorm = firstVal == null ? \"\" : String(firstVal);\n  isUniform = true;\n\n  for (j = 1; j < normalizedRecords.length; j++) {\n    currentVal = normalizedRecords[j][attrKeyLower];\n    currentNorm = currentVal == null ? \"\" : String(currentVal);\n\n    if (currentNorm !== firstNorm) {\n      isUniform = false;\n      break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (preserveKeySet[attrKeyLower]) {\n    // Preserved fields stay in rows regardless; track variance for groupBy.\n    if (!isUniform) {\n      preservedVaryingKeySet[attrKeyLower] = true;\n    }\n    continue;\n  }\n\n  if (isUniform) {\n    repeatAttributes.push({\n      attribute: attrKey,\n      value: firstVal\n    });\n\n    uniformKeySet[attrKeyLower] = true;\n  }\n}\n\n// --- Build pruned records ---\n// Used only if we cannot safely group.\n\nvar prunedRecords = [];\n\nfor (i = 0; i < records.length; i++) {\n  rec = records[i];\n  var pruned = {};\n\n  if (rec && typeof rec === \"object\") {\n    for (k in rec) {\n      if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(rec, k)) {\n        if (!uniformKeySet[String(k).toLowerCase()]) {\n          pruned[k] = rec[k];\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  prunedRecords.push(pruned);\n}\n\n// --- No-groupable-column bypass ----\n\nif (!canGroup) {\n  debug.rollup = {\n    recordCount: records.length,\n    groupCount: prunedRecords.length,\n    groupByKeys: [],\n    rollupFields: rollupFields,\n    repeatAttributes: repeatAttributes,\n    chosenLevel: null,\n    bypassed: true,\n    reason: \"required rollup fields missing: need at least one of BUSINESSUNITNAME/CUSTOMERNAME/ACCOUNTNUMBER/RECEIPTCURRENCYCODE and AMOUNTREMAINING\"\n  };\n\n  return buildOutput(\n    prunedRecords,\n    prunedRecords,\n    repeatAttributes,\n    buildNoRollupSummaryText(prunedRecords, uniformBusinessUnitName),\n    debug\n  );\n}\n\nchosenLevel = businessUnitKey\n  ? \"business_unit_customer_account_receipt_currency\"\n  : \"customer_account_receipt_currency\";\n\n// --- Secondary groupBy: preserved fields that vary across records --------\n// Avoid duplicating RECEIPTCURRENCYCODE if it is already in groupByKeys.\n\nfor (i = 0; i < PRESERVE_FIELDS.length; i++) {\n  var pfLower = String(PRESERVE_FIELDS[i]).toLowerCase();\n\n  if (preservedVaryingKeySet[pfLower]) {\n    var pfActualKey = keyMap[pfLower];\n\n    if (pfActualKey && !containsKeyIgnoreCase(groupByKeys, pfActualKey)) {\n      groupByKeys.push(pfActualKey);\n      forcedGroupKeySet[String(pfActualKey).toLowerCase()] = true;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// --- Date-key detection ---\n// Date fields are excluded from pass-through in aggregated rows because\n// there is no meaningful single-value representation for a group.\n\nvar DATE_KEY_TOKENS = [\n  \"date\",\n  \"datetime\",\n  \"timestamp\",\n  \"time\",\n  \"_dt\",\n  \"dt_\"\n];\n\nfunction isDateKey(lowerName) {\n  for (var d = 0; d < DATE_KEY_TOKENS.length; d++) {\n    if (lowerName.indexOf(DATE_KEY_TOKENS[d]) !== -1) {\n      return true;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return false;\n}\n\n// --- Aggregate ---\n// Output column order:\n//   1. GroupBy dimension keys:\n//      BUSINESSUNITNAME when varying, CUSTOMERNAME, ACCOUNTNUMBER,\n//      RECEIPTCURRENCYCODE, then any varying preserved currency fields.\n//   2. count\n//   3. AMOUNTREMAINING summed and rounded to 2 decimals\n//   4. Pass-through fields that are uniform within the group.\n\nvar groups = {};\n\nfor (i = 0; i < records.length; i++) {\n  rec = normalizedRecords[i];\n\n  var keyParts = [];\n\n  for (j = 0; j < groupByKeys.length; j++) {\n    groupVal = rec[String(groupByKeys[j]).toLowerCase()];\n    keyParts.push(groupVal == null ? \"\" : String(groupVal));\n  }\n\n  groupKey = keyParts.length ? keyParts.join(\"|||\") : \"__TOTAL__\";\n\n  if (!groups[groupKey]) {\n    groups[groupKey] = {\n      count: 0,\n      _tracker: {}\n    };\n\n    // Seed groupBy dimension values.\n    for (j = 0; j < groupByKeys.length; j++) {\n      groups[groupKey][groupByKeys[j]] =\n        rec[String(groupByKeys[j]).toLowerCase()];\n    }\n\n    // Seed rollup accumulators.\n    for (j = 0; j < presentRollups.length; j++) {\n      groups[groupKey][presentRollups[j]] = 0;\n    }\n\n    // Seed pass-through tracker for all remaining eligible fields.\n    var origRec = records[i];\n    var origK, origKLower, isGBKey;\n\n    for (origK in origRec) {\n      if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(origRec, origK)) continue;\n\n      origKLower = String(origK).toLowerCase();\n\n      if (uniformKeySet[origKLower]) continue;\n      if (rollupKeySet[origKLower]) continue;\n      if (isDateKey(origKLower)) continue;\n\n      isGBKey = false;\n\n      for (j = 0; j < groupByKeys.length; j++) {\n        if (String(groupByKeys[j]).toLowerCase() === origKLower) {\n          isGBKey = true;\n          break;\n        }\n      }\n\n      if (isGBKey) continue;\n\n      groups[groupKey]._tracker[origK] = {\n        lower: origKLower,\n        firstVal: rec[origKLower],\n        isUniform: true\n      };\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Accumulate count.\n  groups[groupKey].count = groups[groupKey].count + 1;\n\n  // Accumulate AMOUNTREMAINING.\n  for (j = 0; j < presentRollups.length; j++) {\n    value = rec[String(presentRollups[j]).toLowerCase()];\n    num = Number(value);\n\n    if (value != null && !isNaN(num)) {\n      groups[groupKey][presentRollups[j]] =\n        groups[groupKey][presentRollups[j]] + num;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Update within-group uniformity for pass-through candidates.\n  var tracker = groups[groupKey]._tracker;\n\n  for (var trackedKey in tracker) {\n    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(tracker, trackedKey)) continue;\n\n    var entry = tracker[trackedKey];\n\n    if (!entry.isUniform) continue;\n\n    currentVal = rec[entry.lower];\n    currentNorm = currentVal == null ? \"\" : String(currentVal);\n    firstNorm = entry.firstVal == null ? \"\" : String(entry.firstVal);\n\n    if (currentNorm !== firstNorm) {\n      entry.isUniform = false;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// --- Collect: build output rows in explicit column order ---\n\nfor (k in groups) {\n  if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(groups, k)) continue;\n\n  row = groups[k];\n\n  var orderedRow = {};\n\n  // 1. GroupBy dimension keys.\n  for (i = 0; i < groupByKeys.length; i++) {\n    orderedRow[groupByKeys[i]] = row[groupByKeys[i]];\n  }\n\n  // 2. count.\n  orderedRow.count = row.count;\n\n  // 3. Rollup measures.\n  for (i = 0; i < presentRollups.length; i++) {\n    actualKey = presentRollups[i];\n    orderedRow[actualKey] = Math.round(row[actualKey] * 100) / 100;\n  }\n\n  // 4. Pass-through fields that proved uniform within this group.\n  var rowTracker = row._tracker;\n\n  for (var rowTrackedKey in rowTracker) {\n    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(rowTracker, rowTrackedKey)) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    var te = rowTracker[rowTrackedKey];\n\n    if (te.isUniform) {\n      orderedRow[rowTrackedKey] = te.firstVal;\n    }\n  }\n\n  aggregatedData.push(orderedRow);\n}\n\n// --- Sort descending by count, then AMOUNTREMAINING ---\n\nvar amountRemainingActualKey = presentRollups[0];\n\nfor (i = 0; i < aggregatedData.length - 1; i++) {\n  for (j = i + 1; j < aggregatedData.length; j++) {\n    var shouldSwap = false;\n\n    if (aggregatedData[j].count > aggregatedData[i].count) {\n      shouldSwap = true;\n    } else if (\n      aggregatedData[j].count === aggregatedData[i].count &&\n      Number(aggregatedData[j][amountRemainingActualKey] || 0) >\n        Number(aggregatedData[i][amountRemainingActualKey] || 0)\n    ) {\n      shouldSwap = true;\n    }\n\n    if (shouldSwap) {\n      tempRow = aggregatedData[i];\n      aggregatedData[i] = aggregatedData[j];\n      aggregatedData[j] = tempRow;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// --- Output ---\n\ndebug.rollup = {\n  recordCount: records.length,\n  groupCount: aggregatedData.length,\n  groupByKeys: groupByKeys,\n  rollupFields: rollupFields,\n  repeatAttributes: repeatAttributes,\n  chosenLevel: chosenLevel,\n  threshold: ROLLUP_THRESHOLD,\n  businessUnit: {\n    detected: businessUnitInfo.hasBusinessUnitField,\n    uniform: businessUnitInfo.isUniform,\n    uniformValue: uniformBusinessUnitName,\n    fieldName: businessUnitInfo.fieldName,\n    includedInGrouping: !!businessUnitKey\n  },\n  behavior: \"If recordCount <= threshold, raw pass-through. If over threshold but all records share CUSTOMERNAME and CUSTOMERACCOUNTNUMBER and Business Unit is not varying, rollup is skipped. Otherwise, records are grouped by BUSINESSUNITNAME when varying, CUSTOMERNAME, CUSTOMERACCOUNTNUMBER, and RECEIPTCURRENCYCODE; count is calculated; AMOUNTREMAINING is summed; CASHRECEIPTID is removed before processing.\"\n};\n\nvar summary = buildRollupSummaryText(\n  aggregatedData,\n  records.length,\n  uniformBusinessUnitName\n);\n\nreturn buildOutput(\n  aggregatedData,\n  aggregatedData,\n  repeatAttributes,\n  summary,\n  debug\n);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
